{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/card-sync.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731057Z","id":"487dd91624f77a276deb8f3ecfe7963392c43620da67d0e2082724611e817b40","body":{"detail":"The gallery topic is shared by every viewer, so it cannot carry this viewer's attention (addressed threads, new replies, open threads): a version, thread or thread_deleted event there still fetches the viewer's attention on that one artifact, and a card's roster (participants) is only as fresh as the last full fetch (going live, resync, and every SAFETY_MS).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"7bdd3932434a71d1ad19e2be45e3bcc78fc1aeb1b9b1eb6f901e3465908a0ac1"},"suggested_fix":"A per-viewer topic, or attention computed from the thread summary, would remove the fetch.","summary":"The gallery fetches this viewer's attention per event","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:28.381871Z","id":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"5db66b848687622e5d49e34f29d62226d5e43b73a103486a2ad57576b2d27af4"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewComment.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378103Z","id":"753891e2ec0c63c60fad14a86220781e7be5f417335ad46c5fb85568d52ca61c","body":{"detail":"The box re-implements the stage composer's target line, status line, focus on render, Escape to close, Cmd/Ctrl+Enter to post and the busy state (Composer.svelte). Rendering Composer.svelte from this lazy chunk makes the artifact entry export it, which adds 5 gzip bytes to an entry that sits exactly at its budget (63988 in web/perf/bundle-budget.json, measured by web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs). A behaviour change to the stage composer (a post queued while a screenshot is taken, the keyboard-trail guard, the live status region) must be mirrored here by hand.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"072d1faa169ad8499be271406d7ad89a490cbb4a88f0a1450fc3c964f840da26"},"suggested_fix":"Render Composer.svelte here once the artifact entry has a few bytes of slack, or move Composer.svelte's form into a component both import.","summary":"The New comment box repeats Composer.svelte's form instead of rendering it","tags":["revisit:the artifact entry has slack under its bundle budget","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378379Z","id":"ae1c646c0ce8c2a549174efa8143c36778006cb14a64451371ca253ef652f4e5","body":{"detail":"The panel's first child stays the questions slot (shell/src/sidebar.test.ts 'puts the questions about the page at the top' asserts it), so an agent's question to the viewer still leads; the box comes next, above the working strips, the batch-send button and every thread. Putting the box first means changing that rule and its test.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"fef8ce9785f9ab52019fb078c2e7a3d70f61d7555644dc6354c03c421220d211"},"summary":"The New comment box sits below the questions for the viewer, not first in the panel","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewComment.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:10:14.562354Z","id":"a1183f70422a18f50596fd21afab39b387b08d9efb06a2812ce2fcf243100d3f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ffd6520","summary":"NewComment.svelte now renders Composer.svelte with wholeDraft(); the artifact entry's budget rose by the 18 gzip bytes this costs (63988 to 64006). Evidence: `npx vitest run shell/src/new-comment.test.ts` passes (6 tests, the composer opened in place), `node scripts/bundle-size.mjs` passes at artifact 64006, and e2e/whole-comment.spec.ts passes.","supersedes":"753891e2ec0c63c60fad14a86220781e7be5f417335ad46c5fb85568d52ca61c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:10:14.562538Z","id":"34e47162a05b76ffccf89f11259da17f6f73e72bedf6bea858a49095e6fad068","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Decided by the coordinator of this work: the box stays below the questions slot, since questions to the viewer are time-sensitive and lead the panel. No change.","supersedes":"ae1c646c0ce8c2a549174efa8143c36778006cb14a64451371ca253ef652f4e5","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T06:46:08.079116Z","id":"332f5291ec854a499f7b7a441b855187b49c34da44355e7e451dfaf2a4ac7419","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's agent calls ask; the question reaches Sam's inbox (GET /api/inbox as Sam's cookie lists it) but Sam's shell shows 'The inbox is its owner's' at /inbox and loads no question card, so the agent waits until its timeout. Sam's shell never subscribes to the questions or inbox topic, so Hub::holds_surface for Sam is never true and every hook question of Sam's agents goes to the terminal. The server side (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs, routes/questions.rs) already serves a connected person; no plan task wires the shell for one. Plan Task 21 now carries this: gate the inbox page, the q module and the questions and inbox topics on 'owner or connected person' (a 200 from /api/inbox), verified in a real browser as a person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"4fa564c24b6a3357c8558f6fe29f63e75f25d8a83c205bb99a84e03fb763bc20"},"suggested_fix":"Gate the inbox page and the q module on 'owner or connected person' (GET /api/inbox answering 200 rather than ownerBrowser()), and verify /inbox and a question card in a real browser as a connected person.","summary":"A connected person's browser has no inbox or question surface: /inbox tells them the inbox is the owner's, and the q module loads only for the owner","tags":["review","task:21","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.856081Z","id":"31b2b5407e05366873abebfca2258736dba7844357defeaba91b5e1a253ee62e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","summary":"/people now loads its page the same way (web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts peoplePage, its own chunk, measured as `people` by web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs); no perf gate times /people either.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:21:12.878654Z","id":"8cded220ef0bd2b74b908bca629000487676e98a46f7d27ff459b0153844e82a","body":{"detail":"The banner is a floating pill at the foot of the stage (16px from the bottom), the .banner pattern of theme.css. At the top (where .banner sits by default) it covered the page's heading and, at 390px, the first changed element; the hosted prototype (hosted/ui/src/components/DraftBanner.svelte) is a full-width strip above the frame that takes height from it. The foot can cover a page's last lines and sits where the gesture hint shows.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"644f2b09adf7dcedf95daab24d7542db8db7e82c9a37a148efbeab6614c89fcf"},"summary":"Draft banner at the foot of the stage rather than the top or a strip that pushes the frame down","tags":["drafts","ui","revisit:a page's footer controls are hidden by the banner","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.647490Z","id":"4030afed5afdf271dc22537c9e49bc1157f338b3ec018a7461711e6fc05d8cfa","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8cded220ef0bd2b74b908bca629000487676e98a46f7d27ff459b0153844e82a","summary":"Kept at the foot of the stage, the place branch rust-live-seats gives its spectator banner for the same reason (a top banner hid the page heading); the foot is now one stacking container, .stage-foot (StageIsland.svelte, theme.css), holding the gesture hint and the draft banner so neither covers the other","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.647553Z","id":"7526ffb5df8d2df3fc177d8b654590a3d2cf6562c6dd25a686832b6b951b4bd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a88e5379","summary":"Decided by a88e5379: the banner stays at the stage's foot inside .stage-foot. Browser-checked at 1280 and 390, light and dark (a hint added to .stage-foot sits above the banner, its bottom at or above the banner's top; no horizontal scroll); `npx playwright test e2e/drafts.spec.ts` passes","supersedes":"8cded220ef0bd2b74b908bca629000487676e98a46f7d27ff459b0153844e82a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/StageIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.648984Z","id":"21794a99a26fde0b2a4231041bbdf1cfa7ef184eb9db24533ba8504a9e0dddc1","body":{"detail":"rust-live-seats renders <div class=\"banner spectate\"> in StageIsland.svelte as a sibling of the notice banner, placed by theme.css `.banner.spectate { top: auto; bottom: 16px; z-index: 5 }` (and a 480px rule with left/right 16px). This branch's draft banner sits in .stage-foot, also 16px from the stage's bottom. Move the spectate div inside <div class=\"stage-foot\"> (after the draft banner, or before it to sit above); `.stage-foot > .banner` makes it static, so its bottom/left/right/transform rules go inert and can be dropped.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"48185f62b30f9dab3fe46869f78c48bb69e87ddbdab4c8e996d4b91fcb18865b"},"summary":"Merging rust-live-seats: its spectator banner must move into .stage-foot or it overlaps the draft banner","tags":["drafts","ui","merge","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/StageIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:08.575739Z","id":"08a2346e4e63c593dd20b5ebcbb4e15b6594a324fbba3ef3788f042144006bfa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:83ad7424","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"055d37c636889e67b2609d0bc9ccd1c9b6c9d925268b06dd453ad7efe3c69026"},"summary":"The spectate banner renders inside .stage-foot after the draft banner; theme.css drops its own bottom/left/right/transform placement and stretches it at 480px. Measured with both shown: at 1280x800 the draft banner ends at y=738 and the spectator banner starts at y=746; at 390x844, 711 and 719. e2e/seats.spec.ts and e2e/drafts.spec.ts pass","supersedes":"21794a99a26fde0b2a4231041bbdf1cfa7ef184eb9db24533ba8504a9e0dddc1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:02.671412Z","id":"a4d376824b3e5f61e21fa3da60b170d381d4a4ca12672ba5a4913c3736c5920d","body":{"detail":"A person's pick composer and New comment box both put their draft under thread null, so the sidebar's writers box above the threads shows the name and the text but not the spot; the spot is outlined in the page only (the pick's live selection, web/shell/src/view/live-view.ts sendCursor). Naming the pick's quote or element beside the draft would need the anchor label in the live message.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":208},"content_hash":"28d34fb6d6ebe7773ccca0a659a186acfdc8216af1eadaf1e7686682595fa979"},"summary":"Others' new comments say who writes, not what they are commenting on","tags":["live-layers","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:49:03.386685Z","id":"844c615e910a083e7ad3006cae8c9b68740d6e50dc5129453a04ca3c03fc7699","body":{"detail":"Below 700 px the pill (.who) may shrink with overflow: hidden so the top bar never scrolls sideways (with two people, three agents and '2 viewing' it was 394 px at 390, More pushed off screen). When it shrinks, the end of the pill, the 'N viewing' count and the last chips, is cut off with no sign. Options: drop the count below a width, cap the roster at one chip per side when there is a count, or move the count into the people panel at phone width.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"287c95888790091a5edf54e5d6200b30103768f5eca7a9e4fe919cc2c41c6668"},"summary":"At phone width a crowded people pill is clipped at its right edge, hiding the viewing count without an ellipsis","tags":["ui","phone","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.167408Z","id":"bb5952b279110eb432399d1781ba20bd9405c9fd6dcb56bdb085522d1da5dcce","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9cfb85d5","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"39ac376e501ae839340948c725b0c74fbe8a809c02556d58def8f9d2444bcf45"},"summary":"The inbox page, the q module and the questions and inbox topics load in any browser GET /api/inbox answers (inboxBrowser in web/shell/src/owner.ts), in the gallery and the artifact view. Evidence: gallery.test.ts 'gives a connected person's browser its inbox at /inbox, Inbox in the header, and the inbox and questions topics' passes, and e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts passes: Sam's browser at the LAN address shows his inbox, and his answer to his agent's ask reaches the agent's clax mcp.","supersedes":"332f5291ec854a499f7b7a441b855187b49c34da44355e7e451dfaf2a4ac7419","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.168179Z","id":"b9b2cafad146ac28ee85b03a8e99ec0a102fbfe21d4bee58c39c7ec839ab8be0","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"8562287422b69247ef5172e2996d8000dd4a834547e2eec0f95c600f71de4284"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","supersedes":"4708b4264803165869b7e2a20709b0ed80f387495339ea5ebb29e18a5f66abbb","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815322Z","id":"a41a081a026386a88b9b7c4791858f7a18e9136c79a6a73c6f7927b13532f26d","body":{"detail":"The card is shown while the thread's delivery state is withheld; deciding releases the thread, so the card (and the outcome it shows, \"Allowed in this thread\") disappears with the next thread event, and the label changes to the delivery state. The inbox keeps decided cards in place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"34910f9acc7a57e27bfa368560c2dc444964520c59d09eb71bf5bf41d06e0e87"},"suggested_fix":"Keep a card decided here until the thread is collapsed or the view reloads.","summary":"The approval card above a thread leaves as soon as the decision lands","tags":["task:22","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.162875Z","id":"51447d801fa5818c946632cf7853a6ab0eb7ba16df2e9fbe17d7a07284da5860","body":{"detail":"Failure: a LAN viewer comments on a thread, the owner replies '+1', and the owner sends the thread to Sam's agent (Sam lets the owner's content reach his agents). Sam gets an open routing request for the LAN viewer's comment (GET /api/approvals/requests) and his inbox strip says '2 approvals' for two such threads, but the thread's feedback_state is 'sent': the owner's card reads 'sent, waiting for the agent' and Sam's artifact view shows no approval card above the thread, because the card is gated on feedback_state.state === 'withheld' (here) and the daemon derives that state from the thread's latest forwarded comment only (FEEDBACK_STATES, crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1800-1822). Reproduced in Chromium on a scratch daemon at commit f7a89d53.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"34910f9acc7a57e27bfa368560c2dc444964520c59d09eb71bf5bf41d06e0e87"},"suggested_fix":"Show the card for every open thread with an open approval item for this viewer (thread-approvals.ts already fetches them per artifact), not only withheld ones; and have the thread's delivery state read withheld (with its approver) while any undelivered row of the thread is held under an open request, so the sender sees it too. Add a test with a two-comment thread whose first comment is held.","summary":"A thread whose newest comment reaches the agent hides its open approval request: no approval card above it, and its card reads 'sent, waiting for the agent'","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163617Z","id":"da6f1bf933685f5439c5ccd642c822204ec8e5b31c5a84fb265ce2250a6b7a12","body":{"detail":"The chip is capped at 45% of the card head with an ellipsis; a 32-character agent name ('clax-multi-person-agent-strip-ab') is clipped at 1280 px, and for another person's agent the person after ' · ' is not visible at all at 390 px, where there is no hover. The title is only '<person>'s agent', so the clipped agent name cannot be read anywhere on the card.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"c4e0c89012c6eee44bb22a89549c9a94d4af865540ab76a4a3f1e6175bbff523"},"suggested_fix":"Make the title '<agent name>, <person>'s agent' (or 'your agent'), so hover and assistive tech get the whole name.","summary":"The owner chip's hover text never names the agent, and the chip clips both name and person","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.255042Z","id":"1bd4ebd4d659cd4ddb42d8f9957736b3bf60aa09f9814cc57131b7b9cdf29ad3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"The thread's state reads withheld while any of its rows is held (state_of in crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs looks at every row, not only the newest comment's), and the sidebar puts the approval card above any sent thread with an open request of this viewer's, whatever its state. Evidence: api_approvals::a_thread_waits_for_approval_while_an_earlier_comment_is_held passes (LAN viewer comments, the owner replies '+1', the owner sends to Sam's agent: one request, state withheld, approver Sam), and fails with the old newest-comment-only check; thread-owner.test.ts 'puts the card above a thread whose newest comment went through while an earlier one waits' passes.","supersedes":"51447d801fa5818c946632cf7853a6ab0eb7ba16df2e9fbe17d7a07284da5860","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.257609Z","id":"cbe7729e9446a4831c5098169e7d9b1bb1ce82b0a84fd3a26218b148c6e02a5a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"The chip's title names the agent whole: 'sam-web, Sam's agent' or 'clax-claude, your agent'. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts chip tests and web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts (title 'sam-notes, Sam's agent') pass.","supersedes":"da6f1bf933685f5439c5ccd642c822204ec8e5b31c5a84fb265ce2250a6b7a12","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/thread-approvals.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.261111Z","id":"ebcdef66dfc53597bba1d8df20f8ca720898ee76046645e10c2fb56511ab2687","body":{"detail":"approvalsFor asks /api/inbox?kind=approval&artifact=<aid>&limit=200 and keeps the open ones; on an artifact with more than 200 approval items for this viewer, an older open request gets no card above its thread (the inbox still lists it).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"13ada5962992c59740f6e11d0f02bb133386432bd8365ed150f0f9331aed060c"},"suggested_fix":"Page through next_cursor, or have the inbox list filter approval items by request status.","summary":"The approval card above a thread reads the newest 200 approval items of the artifact, decided ones included","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317399Z","id":"bc8dabfb007596199c7bb9ee34186c202dcd866e3944e5d015cc0f139a8e094f","body":{"detail":"Failure: in Chromium at 390 px, Sam's view of a thread owned by the owner's agent named clax-multi-person shows the chip as 'clax-multi-person · …' (scrollWidth > clientWidth, also at 1280 px); the title 'clax-multi-person, Alex's agent' fixes the hover case (record da6f1bf9, closed by cbe7729e), but phones have no hover, so whose agent owns the thread cannot be read there. The chip is capped at max-width 45% (line 194).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"27e61d3c10a083f476b2a112151790172f0799095acedb50608d859b2ab40a12"},"suggested_fix":"Let the chip wrap below the anchor at narrow widths, or clip the agent name and keep ' · <person>' whole.","summary":"At phone width another person's name on the owner chip is still cut off; only the hover title names it","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SendMenu.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317441Z","id":"a710d7eecc9218b901a639296bbb61efbf8a94b3e52b6336f5b5a5f4d7372f36","body":{"detail":"Failure: a LAN viewer (not connected) opens the Send menu at /a/<aid> and the browser logs 'Failed to load resource: the server responded with a status of 403 (Forbidden)' for GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/approves-first each time. The shell already knows the viewer is neither the owner nor a person (ShellSidebar.svelte tests s.me?.owner || s.me?.person for the approval card).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"33cdbc519d7c246d7aa0d91cd784c4d1093cac91f79b0385e460b50630690b35"},"suggested_fix":"Pass aid/threads to SendButton only when the viewer is the owner or a connected person.","summary":"Every Send menu a LAN viewer opens asks approves-first and logs a 403 to the console","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317485Z","id":"6f57bbe4361a76c8da5c1b9612b7f832e0e676bf4afd69019bf4bc6fdb2ec3ff","body":{"detail":"Failure: the owner on an artifact where only Sam's agent is live, with two unsent threads, sees no send-unsent button (Chromium 1280 and 390 px); each card's Send and the selection bar's 'Send 2 to …' open the menu, but sending all unsent needs ticking every card. The `!pick` guard hides the button instead of letting it open the same menu.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":222},"end":{"line":222},"content_hash":"5afef93bda6e86ed7909748b307da430ec354804c2a44df3cb682934a86b0fc8"},"summary":"With only other people's agents live, the 'Send N unsent' button is gone rather than opening the menu","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"e176c69ecad624feebfeeb2f5d53fc02bc872b7ed695f77504ff7f0d3f4f597b","body":{"detail":"A person's pick composer and New comment box both put their draft under thread null, so the sidebar's writers box above the threads shows the name and the text but not the spot; the spot is outlined in the page only (the pick's live selection, web/shell/src/view/live-view.ts sendCursor). Naming the pick's quote or element beside the draft would need the anchor label in the live message.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":226},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"28d34fb6d6ebe7773ccca0a659a186acfdc8216af1eadaf1e7686682595fa979"},"summary":"Others' new comments say who writes, not what they are commenting on","supersedes":"a4d376824b3e5f61e21fa3da60b170d381d4a4ca12672ba5a4913c3736c5920d","tags":["live-layers","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"ed95ead8f0d830facc04622854415fa962f9cec9c747915ce56c1d6df667fc77","body":{"detail":"Failure: in Chromium at 390 px, Sam's view of a thread owned by the owner's agent named clax-multi-person shows the chip as 'clax-multi-person · …' (scrollWidth > clientWidth, also at 1280 px); the title 'clax-multi-person, Alex's agent' fixes the hover case (record da6f1bf9, closed by cbe7729e), but phones have no hover, so whose agent owns the thread cannot be read there. The chip is capped at max-width 45% (line 194).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":179},"content_hash":"27e61d3c10a083f476b2a112151790172f0799095acedb50608d859b2ab40a12"},"suggested_fix":"Let the chip wrap below the anchor at narrow widths, or clip the agent name and keep ' · <person>' whole.","summary":"At phone width another person's name on the owner chip is still cut off; only the hover title names it","supersedes":"bc8dabfb007596199c7bb9ee34186c202dcd866e3944e5d015cc0f139a8e094f","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"ce0922d0c368a754793f82175342c92ecf9377e42204310df000e1e00ae1eaef","body":{"detail":"Below 700 px the pill (.who) may shrink with overflow: hidden so the top bar never scrolls sideways (with two people, three agents and '2 viewing' it was 394 px at 390, More pushed off screen). When it shrinks, the end of the pill, the 'N viewing' count and the last chips, is cut off with no sign. Options: drop the count below a width, cap the roster at one chip per side when there is a count, or move the count into the people panel at phone width.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"287c95888790091a5edf54e5d6200b30103768f5eca7a9e4fe919cc2c41c6668"},"summary":"At phone width a crowded people pill is clipped at its right edge, hiding the viewing count without an ellipsis","supersedes":"844c615e910a083e7ad3006cae8c9b68740d6e50dc5129453a04ca3c03fc7699","tags":["ui","phone","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"9707ea366fbf1f769915443fcab1a9779d8d3467e65af416f7c3472f23daec18","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"949ee66fbd902fe13b7116a027c0786aa4b813eb96be329d49c4922c2eac27cc"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","supersedes":"b9b2cafad146ac28ee85b03a8e99ec0a102fbfe21d4bee58c39c7ec839ab8be0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:41.935654Z","id":"fefd8d61ea66b578f29354e0cf77096dc743374838aba428d18dece9e2b378fd","body":{"detail":"Failure: the owner on an artifact where only Sam's agent is live, with two unsent threads, sees no send-unsent button (Chromium 1280 and 390 px); each card's Send and the selection bar's 'Send 2 to …' open the menu, but sending all unsent needs ticking every card. The `!pick` guard hides the button instead of letting it open the same menu.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":232},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"cd09e7a9f4b87dd272c347479f75eec6ab3a4bee1f0e48a3feaf8696f6941321"},"summary":"With only other people's agents live, the 'Send N unsent' button is gone rather than opening the menu","supersedes":"6f57bbe4361a76c8da5c1b9612b7f832e0e676bf4afd69019bf4bc6fdb2ec3ff","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:41.935654Z","id":"cb998259585aedc7e406cc2a6c766dbacdf1754811aea4dd027a8c901e13ff45","body":{"detail":"The card is shown while the thread's delivery state is withheld; deciding releases the thread, so the card (and the outcome it shows, \"Allowed in this thread\") disappears with the next thread event, and the label changes to the delivery state. The inbox keeps decided cards in place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"6dff1646984c1a4b12213e009b773e3db44fdd942f8489665c6e24c3d58ce30a"},"suggested_fix":"Keep a card decided here until the thread is collapsed or the view reloads.","summary":"The approval card above a thread leaves as soon as the decision lands","supersedes":"a41a081a026386a88b9b7c4791858f7a18e9136c79a6a73c6f7927b13532f26d","tags":["task:22","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.268853Z","id":"1472fc0cad9c4d1e801867fa41d307b3d59772bb3dc06f0ce8f200a0c8647eec","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"cb998259585aedc7e406cc2a6c766dbacdf1754811aea4dd027a8c901e13ff45","summary":"Changed since recorded: the card above a thread is now shown while the thread is open and sent to an agent, to the owner or a connected person (web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte:33), not only while its delivery state is withheld, so a decision no longer removes it at the next thread event. Proposed close: reason:fixed, once someone confirms the decided card stays in a browser.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.660616Z","id":"98acc0e2e23308fe05f933939943e555c934e59c02bec4b8950b236db8b2041c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"The chip's agent name gives way (ellipsis) and ' · <person>' stays whole. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'lets the person on another person's agent's chip stay whole' passes; Chromium at 390 px shows 'clax-multi-person-… · Sam' (target/t22/shots-r2/owner-after-decline-long-chip-390-*).","supersedes":"bc8dabfb007596199c7bb9ee34186c202dcd866e3944e5d015cc0f139a8e094f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SendMenu.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.663322Z","id":"cdb9c60248fd8bdd74e300c0bfecf57b174db48e9fafd473ce7ba8a47b0b634f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"The sidebar hands SendButton the artifact to ask about only in the owner's or a connected person's browser. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'never asks who approves first in a browser that may not learn it' passes; web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts sees no approves-first request from the LAN viewer's menu.","supersedes":"a710d7eecc9218b901a639296bbb61efbf8a94b3e52b6336f5b5a5f4d7372f36","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.664240Z","id":"f036f9e5bdec61556b7b53479d475ae96e212e70e9991d881c4b74982c49dbfd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"With no target chosen, the unsent bar is a Send button that opens the menu ('Send 2 unsent to …'). Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'with only other people's agents live and no target' passes (the bar opens the menu); Chromium: target/t22/shots-r2/owner-unsent-bar-opens-menu-*.","supersedes":"6f57bbe4361a76c8da5c1b9612b7f832e0e676bf4afd69019bf4bc6fdb2ec3ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657901Z","id":"cea8f8405733d61b549c25a3dddbb722ddee67727b7691afee0f9c8bd6a1e837","body":{"detail":"The label takes 'yours' (an open request of this viewer's on the thread) over the thread's feedback_state. Routing requests outlive their target (spec section 9.2 withdraws them only on resolve, delete, revocation, or the end of an asking session). Seen as the owner: (1) after the owner's codex session that Mia's thread waited for ended, the owner read 'waiting for your approval', and every other viewer read 'agent session ended; waiting for a new one'; (2) after the owner's claude agent handed Mia's thread to Sam's agent, the owner read 'waiting for your approval', while the server state was 'waiting for Sam's approval'. The server state follows StateRow::waits_for_approval (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1855-1867), which needs a live session. The approver's label does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"cc55684f277b54f807d8f3b1642d19c5389486e04176b23d17e46f36ada43d4f"},"summary":"The approver's card reads 'waiting for your approval' after the target session ended or the thread was handed off","tags":["review","people","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657949Z","id":"466b955af142f500e9759bebec441475f8de029fd47f0414f41222ebe3c2beac","body":{"detail":"Chromium at 1280 px, as the owner, once the Inbox button loads. The summary line '8 open threads · clax-multi-person-claude (Mia's), clax-multi-person (Sam's) idle' takes 444 px. It is white-space: nowrap, with no min-width: 0 or ellipsis. The page is 1298 px wide, and the theme switch is pushed 18 px past the viewport. At 1440 px it fits. Default agent names come from the repository and branch, so names this long are usual.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"fe41b1e8a8b817ef590fc159804a36aae40c8d69b9a5a193a2f281f911c3ae0d"},"summary":"The top bar overflows at 1280 px when the agent summary names two other people's agents","tags":["review","ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.889711Z","id":"1ef2dac15e3c2dc586efd47026c50de50840b1d2236c1ced05054cfdc57162f5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"The card reads the daemon's state only; 'waiting for your approval' comes from the state's mine flag, which the daemon sets only while a live session waits for this viewer's approval. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'reads the daemon's state, not the card above, once nothing waits for this viewer (an ended session, a handoff)' passes.","supersedes":"cea8f8405733d61b549c25a3dddbb722ddee67727b7691afee0f9c8bd6a1e837","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.890620Z","id":"ae2a7ade4ab987884c3f5fbc7794c3595385955c01f55e4888dbc2a6bfbbfe70","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"The summary can shrink (flex 0 1 auto, min-width 0, ellipsis on both lines). Evidence: Chromium at 1280 px with the owner's, Sam's (clax-multi-person) and Mia's (clax-multi-person-claude) agents shows no page overflow and the summary ending in an ellipsis (target/t22/shots-r3/declined-owner-1280-light.png; the run logged no sideways scroll).","supersedes":"466b955af142f500e9759bebec441475f8de029fd47f0414f41222ebe3c2beac","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PeoplePanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:10:35.648631Z","id":"1d44bae3d91159ddb82b5663847b3f586994ce3c86ce63d580f17f7a4fdff711","body":{"detail":"Raise on this artifact shows on the panel's agent rows whose handle GET /api/people/me/raises?artifact= lists in raisable: the artifact's live participant agents (owner, watchers, publishers and commenters, crates/clax-core/src/store/attention.rs participants) of connected machines. PUT /api/agents/<handle>/elevate takes any live agent's handle from a creator, but a person sees other people's agents' handles only where the artifact's participants carry them, so an agent that has not touched the artifact cannot be raised from the shell. A picker of every live agent of a connected machine would show a person other people's agent handles that GET /api/agents keeps from them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"69d4b0a65f09ea34a96bdf9ecf16ff0a4d69693beceda730e905f0d563456707"},"summary":"The artifact's People panel offers a creator's raise only on agents already on the artifact","tags":["revisit:a creator needs to raise an agent before it watches, publishes or comments on their artifact","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/RaiseHere.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:10:35.648699Z","id":"5f863931090360a9e73a4c41c2ad694ebc940ab5ac128805515176d685daf230","body":{"detail":"creatorCaps (web/shell/src/people/model.ts) offers every action the creator holds at the artifact (holds from GET /api/people/me/raises), checked where the creator's own elevation raises it. The creator cannot read another person's agent's rights, so for a Collaborator's agent 'Read artifacts' or 'Comment' shows unchecked although the agent may already do it; checking it changes nothing the agent can do, and the agent's person's People shows it as raised. The raises route could also answer which of holds the agent lacks, at the cost of telling the creator part of another person's rights and narrowing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"7534779dd17eeb87fce4f3b401dab7fa11cd27be89c6983d3e34acbdc24e8cbb"},"summary":"A creator's raise lists actions the agent may already hold through its own person's rights","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/RaiseHere.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:59.886269Z","id":"5691d4a6f40ce7a9a8a5b53958ed3a0e0115f405a6d0b488c584a787654d6b20","body":{"detail":"RaiseHere keeps the creator's raise (`mine`) from when the panel loaded and never re-reads it: persons have no People topic, and change() reloads only on success. After Mia (the agent's person) or the owner removes Sam's raise (DELETE ?granter=), Sam's open panel still reads 'Raise on this artifact (raised)' with every box checked. When Sam then unchecks one box to give less, change() PUTs `elevation({elevate: mine}, key, false)`, the stale raise minus that action, and PUT replaces the granter's raise whole (spec §7.4), so the rest of the removed raise is stored again with no error. Reproduced on a scratch daemon: Mia removed the owner's raise, the owner removed Sam's update+delete+db-admin raise on notes-fix (audit seq 54, 55, reasons removed_by_person, removed_by_owner); Sam unchecked 'Delete artifacts' in the panel he had opened before, and audit seq 56 recorded Sam raising notes-fix again with update and db read/write at admin. Spec §7.4 lets the granter raise again, but here the creator meant to take away and the removal by the person, who answers for the agent (owner decision 'Both may remove'), is undone without either of them seeing it. Separately, the panel's note (line 45) says the raise lasts 'until its session ends', and does not say that the agent's person or the owner may remove it or that the person's narrowing caps it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"11b9a3ae061a531f1b47f569fdab9c8229db3067bc7bac662165e76c23e60ac0"},"suggested_fix":"Re-read GET /api/people/me/raises?artifact= before applying a change, and treat a 404 not_raised or a raise that differs from `mine` as 'removed by someone else' (reload and say so) instead of PUTting the stale set; or make PUT conditional on the raise the client saw. Mention removal and capping in the note.","summary":"A creator's stale Raise panel silently restores a raise the agent's person or the owner removed","tags":["review","security","t20b-rereview","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/RaiseHere.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:02:24.341350Z","id":"84119812a70c3f80a8bef6603f0c6280bc3abb37cdf43408d8371e5b49f27070","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:702d726c","summary":"Fixed: every raise carries a version (crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs, new at each change); PUT /api/agents/<handle>/elevate takes if_version and answers 409 conflict with the raise as it stands, writing and recording nothing (Store::elevate_agent_if); RaiseHere.svelte always sends it, PeoplePanel.svelte reads the raises again when the raise panel opens and when the page regains focus, and on a conflict the panel shows the raise as it stands with a note. Evidence: api_people::a_stale_creators_change_never_restores_a_removed_raise passes (Mia removes, then Sam's panel built on v1 unchecks Delete: 409, raise null, no agent.elevate row, no generation bump, Mia's agent still refused; then the owner removes a later raise and the stale v3 change is refused too); people-panel.test.ts 'is refused when the raise it was built on was removed since' passes; mutations dropping the version check, reusing one version, dropping if_version from the panel and dropping the focus refresh each fail a test; in Chromium at 1280 and 390, light and dark, Sam's open panel after Mia's Remove showed the note and no raise (target/t20b/shots/creator-stale-*).","supersedes":"5691d4a6f40ce7a9a8a5b53958ed3a0e0115f405a6d0b488c584a787654d6b20","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/RaiseHere.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:06:18.547767Z","id":"3dda06f0c462be544d353399cbbe92eba17bc7ca0044876a8e61ec4d75730461","body":{"detail":"creatorCaps (web/shell/src/people/model.ts) offers every action the creator holds at the artifact (holds from GET /api/people/me/raises), checked where the creator's own elevation raises it. The creator cannot read another person's agent's rights, so for a Collaborator's agent 'Read artifacts' or 'Comment' shows unchecked although the agent may already do it; checking it changes nothing the agent can do, and the agent's person's People shows it as raised. The raises route could also answer which of holds the agent lacks, at the cost of telling the creator part of another person's rights and narrowing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"7534779dd17eeb87fce4f3b401dab7fa11cd27be89c6983d3e34acbdc24e8cbb"},"summary":"A creator's raise lists actions the agent may already hold through its own person's rights","supersedes":"5f863931090360a9e73a4c41c2ad694ebc940ab5ac128805515176d685daf230","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PeoplePanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:06:18.551135Z","id":"a134ba4e7093ccf23481e64255485b200a8f3fed3043987c235db77c8a79edbf","body":{"detail":"Raise on this artifact shows on the panel's agent rows whose handle GET /api/people/me/raises?artifact= lists in raisable: the artifact's live participant agents (owner, watchers, publishers and commenters, crates/clax-core/src/store/attention.rs participants) of connected machines. PUT /api/agents/<handle>/elevate takes any live agent's handle from a creator, but a person sees other people's agents' handles only where the artifact's participants carry them, so an agent that has not touched the artifact cannot be raised from the shell. A picker of every live agent of a connected machine would show a person other people's agent handles that GET /api/agents keeps from them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":169},"content_hash":"362eacba60d68d0924d120d7dbdd30daca5b905a20d858c78b819e455bc026d6"},"summary":"The artifact's People panel offers a creator's raise only on agents already on the artifact","supersedes":"1d44bae3d91159ddb82b5663847b3f586994ce3c86ce63d580f17f7a4fdff711","tags":["revisit:a creator needs to raise an agent before it watches, publishes or comments on their artifact","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadApproval.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594250Z","id":"c561421c58f78edc7c9f273c77d320713a16ed9bb5bbdc91233d69079f28d0e5","body":{"detail":"ApprovalCard.svelte:95 keeps focus on the card after a decision, but ThreadApproval refetches when the thread's delivery state changes and, the request no longer open, renders nothing: the focused card is removed. Measured in Chromium as Sam on the artifact view: after pressing \"Allow this thread, including later replies\" on the card above thread 1, document.activeElement is BODY. A keyboard or screen-reader user loses their place in the threads panel.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"c4e41d1ef98bac2fa0c175422a75a2f342bfbef1e48f5d83656119cc01cbdc8e"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the decided card until the next interaction, or move focus to the thread card it stood above.","summary":"Deciding an approval card above a thread drops the keyboard's focus to the page body","tags":["review","final-review-ui","a11y","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SendMenu.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594582Z","id":"7f48f0502fe45e522a0790d8ce8b8ed4ac4f3f4405a63320cbea917c48cdfdc7","body":{"detail":"Opened from the keyboard (caret, Enter), focus stays on the caret; ArrowDown does nothing; Escape is handled only inside the menu, so with focus on the caret the menu stays open. Measured as the owner, Mia and a LAN viewer. Main's menu behaved the same; the menu now carries person groups and \"Sam approves first\" notes, which keyboard users reach only by Tab.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"ec6fcbeeafe9127c405a60e46becaf729b7c5571d223957ecd3c90bf8592db57"},"summary":"The Send menu is role=menu but takes no arrow keys, and Escape on the caret does not close it","tags":["review","final-review-ui","a11y","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/RaiseHere.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594607Z","id":"c7ad81a42e9ae652168d45d5a09473c70e55291aac1af2f8bb9f7c18eb3c53d7","body":{"detail":"`display: flex` on the summary drops Chrome's list-item ::marker, so the expandable section looks like a coloured label; People's own summaries (\"Raise this agent\", \"What this agent may do\") keep the triangle.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":68},"content_hash":"df9bae89df9bc422c9d9fdf64a1ef1f8899e701d776a479decbec2da7602c851"},"summary":"\"Raise on this artifact\" shows no disclosure marker","tags":["review","final-review-ui","styling","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadApproval.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.307824Z","id":"0b40d5ec0b44e20eff3ab870e3dee2109db6ff32692c28c57e5ab7c298321b25","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3724ee8f","summary":"ThreadApproval moves the focus to its thread's card head when the decided card goes. Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'gives the keyboard's focus to the thread's card head once the decided card goes' passes; Chromium as Sam, pressing Enter on 'Allow this thread' above Mia's thread leaves document.activeElement = BUTTON.card-head of that thread.","supersedes":"c561421c58f78edc7c9f273c77d320713a16ed9bb5bbdc91233d69079f28d0e5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SendMenu.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.309799Z","id":"177c73af9c73259c1cc52b8ca8342b8686a43d8fb4be00c604a35a4ed96debff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3724ee8f","summary":"SendMenu takes the focus on open (checked agent, else first), moves with ArrowUp/ArrowDown/Home/End, closes on Escape in it or on the button beside it with focus back on that button, and closes on Tab out. Evidence: send-menu.test.ts 'takes the keyboard...' passes; Chromium as the owner: Enter on the caret focuses 'claude', ArrowDown 'sam-notes', Escape closes it with focus on the caret.","supersedes":"7f48f0502fe45e522a0790d8ce8b8ed4ac4f3f4405a63320cbea917c48cdfdc7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/RaiseHere.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.324664Z","id":"8496393b2aa69ae86d6ff256b1919926853ccc29c118127b513d9e3d55163801","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2eb5ce4a","summary":"The RaiseHere summary is display: list-item, so its disclosure marker shows. Evidence: Chromium screenshots of the owner's People panel at 1280 and 390, light and dark, show the triangle beside 'Raise on this artifact'.","supersedes":"c7ad81a42e9ae652168d45d5a09473c70e55291aac1af2f8bb9f7c18eb3c53d7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Share.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:59:09.396129Z","id":"80f9b7c21dedfd94fab5ffe067c29c7d32bc92184de7d0743b990e886811c241","body":{"detail":"Share.svelte loads with the more menu after the first paint and asks sharing to decide whether to show Share. On a local daemon, which serves no /api/hosted route, that is one 404 per artifact view; on a hosted daemon one store read. It does not delay the first paint or comment mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"dbb107e1fe91721b632d7ece169ed3e065c0c10f9e6a63da75c13119b7805725"},"suggested_fix":"Carry can_share on GET /api/artifacts/<id> (the view already loads it) and drop the separate request.","summary":"Every artifact view asks GET /api/hosted/artifacts/<id>/sharing once after the first paint, and a local daemon answers it 404","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:02:00.328712Z","id":"903491c860e4af2a3f33f9e809674bb491e50dbd4f9ad04352c58ccc1029f587","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49afc8a7","summary":"Fixed: past two idle agents the summary gives their count, the pill shrinks first (flex-shrink 1000, overflow hidden, ellipsis on both lines), and the title keeps min(200px, 20vw) wider than a phone. Evidence: npx playwright test e2e/who-overflow.spec.ts passes (six watching agents named clax-multi-person-reviewer-N: document scrollWidth within the window at 1280 and 390, light and dark; the pill's right edge within 1280); npx vitest run passes 1639.","supersedes":"466b955af142f500e9759bebec441475f8de029fd47f0414f41222ebe3c2beac","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PeoplePanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T18:23:57.774537Z","id":"68b1bc911b2fec12f8f4a4ea93ef19d4197b28194810e8bce37f551b0170ba33","body":{"detail":"participants.agents keeps the sessions that published a version after they end (live: false, docs/contract.md \"agents are the artifact's owner session, its watchers and the sessions that published its versions\"), and the top bar's Roster still shows their chip. idleLine() labels such an agent \"Idle.\" (or \"Idle. Addressed ... in vN.\"), the same as a live one, while the pill's summary line, which filters on live, no longer names it. Observed on a hosted daemon after DELETE /mcp/json ended a member agent's session that had published v2; main renders the same. Decide whether an ended agent should read as ended (or leave the roster).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":98},"content_hash":"0dc6f37a7da5f2bd77250116b167a1056881eedc37e304f7e35cfc21057c39d9"},"summary":"An agent whose session ended reads as Idle in the People and agents panel","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PeoplePanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T03:24:58.795287Z","id":"371508281e94fd905a391a5d6b9672272021ff8902f218546e19350ab9915c70","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c5668e04","summary":"status:decided: the owner decided an agent whose session ended shows as Ended under an Earlier heading, and never counts in the top bar's idle summary. Evidence: npx vitest run shell/src/people-panel.test.ts passes 'lists an agent whose session ended under Earlier, as Ended, never as Idle'; the idle summary already counts live agents only (web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte); e2e/who-overflow.spec.ts passes.","supersedes":"68b1bc911b2fec12f8f4a4ea93ef19d4197b28194810e8bce37f551b0170ba33","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PeoplePanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.253990Z","id":"7f45592f13d70f260965c9fc81cd84a0d9d4667d6eb4bcb4e39ef786517baae2","body":{"detail":"Raise on this artifact shows on the panel's agent rows whose handle GET /api/people/me/raises?artifact= lists in raisable: the artifact's live participant agents (owner, watchers, publishers and commenters, crates/clax-core/src/store/attention.rs participants) of connected machines. PUT /api/agents/<handle>/elevate takes any live agent's handle from a creator, but a person sees other people's agents' handles only where the artifact's participants carry them, so an agent that has not touched the artifact cannot be raised from the shell. A picker of every live agent of a connected machine would show a person other people's agent handles that GET /api/agents keeps from them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":194},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"362eacba60d68d0924d120d7dbdd30daca5b905a20d858c78b819e455bc026d6"},"summary":"The artifact's People panel offers a creator's raise only on agents already on the artifact","supersedes":"a134ba4e7093ccf23481e64255485b200a8f3fed3043987c235db77c8a79edbf","tags":["revisit:a creator needs to raise an agent before it watches, publishes or comments on their artifact","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.268010Z","id":"00f770eed9b3caf67cd64dc137cd5ac1af16c0ee249e033ed59ef71f23b18caf","body":{"detail":"A person's pick composer and New comment box both put their draft under thread null, so the sidebar's writers box above the threads shows the name and the text but not the spot; the spot is outlined in the page only (the pick's live selection, web/shell/src/view/live-view.ts sendCursor). Naming the pick's quote or element beside the draft would need the anchor label in the live message.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":231},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"28d34fb6d6ebe7773ccca0a659a186acfdc8216af1eadaf1e7686682595fa979"},"summary":"Others' new comments say who writes, not what they are commenting on","supersedes":"e176c69ecad624feebfeeb2f5d53fc02bc872b7ed695f77504ff7f0d3f4f597b","tags":["live-layers","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.281780Z","id":"e5e0475f1ae5bd3a66d9fb8b0908587667586076d1b8277c1d770842b6af097e","body":{"detail":"Below 700 px the pill (.who) may shrink with overflow: hidden so the top bar never scrolls sideways (with two people, three agents and '2 viewing' it was 394 px at 390, More pushed off screen). When it shrinks, the end of the pill, the 'N viewing' count and the last chips, is cut off with no sign. Options: drop the count below a width, cap the roster at one chip per side when there is a count, or move the count into the people panel at phone width.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"287c95888790091a5edf54e5d6200b30103768f5eca7a9e4fe919cc2c41c6668"},"summary":"At phone width a crowded people pill is clipped at its right edge, hiding the viewing count without an ellipsis","supersedes":"ce0922d0c368a754793f82175342c92ecf9377e42204310df000e1e00ae1eaef","tags":["ui","phone","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PeoplePanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:31:43.898668Z","id":"18933d0d47687768110450e1e0f9db86ea371227ecd0df4a88d8cd1392df8539","body":{"detail":"The panel passes agentMark the shown name from agentNames (web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts:22), which for a relayed agent is shownName(name, via), 'claude · via Ada's Clax'; agentMark splits on whitespace and takes 'c' and '·'. The roster (web/shell/src/ui/Roster.svelte) marks the same agent from its bare name, 'cl'. The ended row at line 171 does the same.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":182},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"977967a2c596e0bbe8c30977c890aa3536a9406d832a4ad53ccfcda056a36c1d"},"suggested_fix":"Mark from the agent's own name (parts.agents' name or harness), not the shown name, in both rows.","summary":"An agent another Clax relays for is marked 'c·' in the people panel where the roster marks it 'cl'","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:31:43.899314Z","id":"0921100ab9165436c464770b4f4e91b705d931d3874522b870047ad801ef4fde","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"cb998259585aedc7e406cc2a6c766dbacdf1754811aea4dd027a8c901e13ff45","summary":"The decided card still leaves at the thread's next change: ThreadApproval.svelte refetches on each delivery-state change and keeps only open requests (approvalFor), so once Sam allows the thread and his agent reads it, the card is gone. web/e2e/visibility.spec.ts now checks that it has left (expect(.thread-approval .acard).toHaveCount(0)) and reads the decision from GET /api/approvals/requests, since the outcome line could go before it was read under load.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T17:46:26.995925Z","id":"11ec1fc2f956357cbb2738f5c6f4f1496dc588bfc7e409a2cea8c9d71cbe914f","body":{"detail":"The .thread-q-slot sits inside the {:else} branch of {#if !open} (ThreadCard.svelte:152), so a folded card renders no slot. The question is left out of the sidebar's cards (SidebarQuestions.svelte filters out inThread questions) and appears only as a ThreadLinks link. That link's go() (web/shell/src/q/ThreadLinks.svelte) finds no slot, so it follows href ?thread=<id>, which reloads the page. Whether that reload opens or selects the thread has not been checked in a browser.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"0f9d1d8d2cb1f14165df97b481bece02cc05ec62b08f1fc623628cc610c264a8"},"suggested_fix":"Render the slot in the folded summary too, or have the link unfold the card (as clicking a far card's head does) before it scrolls.","summary":"A question asked in a folded (far) thread card has no slot, so it shows nowhere until the card opens","tags":["ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ThreadCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:21:19.079804Z","id":"c269e7245906f0e48d8c763b1e0ba2d1f821003591713d59d4e98bd57f31d28d","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/q/ThreadLinks.svelte go() clicks a folded card's .card-head, waits for its slot's .qcard, scrolls the slot into view and focuses it. web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts reads ?thread=<id> and opens that thread (openPin) once the frame greets, then scrolls its card into view. Passing in just web-test at 0b7e4d15e (//web:unit 1718 passed): thread-questions.test.ts 'opens a folded thread card from its link, then scrolls to its question and focuses it'; artifact-controller.test.ts 'opens the thread the address names once its page greets, and brings its card into view when it renders'.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1acef28e4","summary":"ThreadLinks opens a folded card from its link and focuses its question; the artifact view opens the thread ?thread= names","supersedes":"11ec1fc2f956357cbb2738f5c6f4f1496dc588bfc7e409a2cea8c9d71cbe914f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:00:51.339558Z","id":"8110df92db4e67756bde8ddbbebf2190f3514d4250b5b224688fd82ec4d2f93d","body":{"detail":"InboxPage moved out of the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts) into its own chunk, imported by web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts inboxPage() and started beside q() in loadQ, so the questions budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json, 16384; now 14202) has room for the multi-question card. The two imports run in parallel, so no request waits on another, but web/perf/usable.perf.ts has no /inbox gate to show the time to usable is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"5ca9f876fc11d265f350e6a4b11b062ee39346ecfb1863e72411a4f424017f50"},"suggested_fix":"Add an /inbox first-usable measurement to web/perf/usable.perf.ts.","summary":"/inbox now loads its page as a chunk of its own beside the q module, and no perf gate times /inbox","supersedes":"9707ea366fbf1f769915443fcab1a9779d8d3467e65af416f7c3472f23daec18","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:01:13.074121Z","id":"0c8abc49f74df7b19236062bc0e539be96064fcdefe92831a5e3eeac92b14369","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8110df92db4e67756bde8ddbbebf2190f3514d4250b5b224688fd82ec4d2f93d","summary":"/ now loads the gallery's unread summary (web/shell/src/q/GallerySummary.svelte) the same way: web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts summary(), in loadQ's Promise.all beside q() (git:00d63fea2). web/perf/usable.perf.ts times only the artifact view, so neither /inbox nor the summary on / is timed.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PromptDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:15:38.577174Z","id":"fff04d3f01fa82dc2b79abbfe527a7a6d3c2068b9e65e4169cbafd4cc444ddfe","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the macOS debug app at 647958f22844 (flutter test -d macos driving AppRoot with the real daemon and WebViewAppSurface), make a run log app with one run, then make a dashboard that declares {\"db\":{\"read\":[\"<run log ID>\"]}} and reads it with db.artifact(<ID>).collection('runs').onSnapshot. The consent dialog opens at once ('Let “Weekly Running Total” read “Run Log”'s data?'), but its Allow button stays disabled for the full 20 s watched. A click on Allow (pointer attested through claxHost, real NSEvent click) leaves the dialog open, still disarmed. The page's document.visibilityState reads 'hidden' in the app's WKWebView. Arming waits for two requestAnimationFrame callbacks (lines 53-57), and WebKit does not run them for a page it treats as hidden, so 'armed' never turns true. The host-driven visibility of 647958f22844 covers the event stream only. Seen in a live claude -p run (dashboard bw4hp07d06qe reading d1g80m7k8e79: no armed dialog within 60 s) and reproduced with recorded results and no model call. The same dashboard opened in Chromium against the same daemon shows the dialog normally. Whether a frontmost, unobscured app window also reads hidden is unverified.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"79ea78cb8ec723260f4d109b87f01fd59147196e153e4f5aa5008a93ee3ff9f5"},"suggested_fix":"In app mode, arm Allow from a timer started when the host reports the page visible (claxHost.setVisible) rather than from animation frames, or fall back to a timer when document.visibilityState is hidden. Extend apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart with a cross-app read that allows the dialog inside the hidden WebView.","summary":"In the macOS app the consent dialog's Allow never arms, so an app that reads another app's data cannot be allowed","tags":["live-run","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PromptDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:23:13.632964Z","id":"e003b7a2083d2749786967c78fbe4c5cd38856df2b05fcba0b83790fdb4c1757","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"fff04d3f01fa82dc2b79abbfe527a7a6d3c2068b9e65e4169cbafd4cc444ddfe","summary":"Reproduced by apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart (f1c07f346b12, the cross-app read step): a scripted second app declaring {\"db\":{\"read\":[<run log>]}} opens, the shell's consent dialog appears, and .prompt button.primary stays disabled for the whole 45 s wait; the test fails with 'timed out waiting for the consent dialog's Allow armed (last seen: Allow disabled)'. Run on 647958f22844 with the embedded clax rebuilt by just app-clax macos; the shell document reads visibilityState 'hidden' in that WebView. Once Allow arms, the test clicks it with a real NSEvent click and asserts the page's read (status ok, '5 km logged') and GET /api/artifacts/<reader>/db-grants listing the run log.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PromptDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:28:32.952952Z","id":"1a48f8685e88fb6bb6695f5e248167f84edab7447f32737bd3227d0cd30b2d27","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: PromptDialog arms Allow through nextFrame(…, true), which falls back to a 100 ms timer while the app's host says the page is shown; ALLOW_DELAY_MS kept. Evidence: shell/src/prompt.test.ts 'arms Allow where no animation frame comes while the app's host says the page is shown...' and 'never arms Allow without a frame outside the app' pass; e2e/inter-app.spec.ts 'with no animation frames (the macOS app's WebView), the consent dialog's Allow still arms and the read succeeds' passes (rAF overridden to never call back); vitest 1555/1555. Audit of the other rAF waits recorded on web/shell/src/view/after-paint.ts","supersedes":"fff04d3f01fa82dc2b79abbfe527a7a6d3c2068b9e65e4169cbafd4cc444ddfe","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PromptDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:31:41.395574Z","id":"b6871c2a91d5662e04a850c2e4fbf01b83253f01d010685efbde01341ca9eedb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"1a48f8685e88fb6bb6695f5e248167f84edab7447f32737bd3227d0cd30b2d27","summary":"Verified by apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart (f1c07f346b12) on 647958f22844 (with 647958f22844), embedded clax rebuilt by just app-clax macos: the consent dialog arms Allow, a real NSEvent click on it grants the read, the reader page reports {status: ok, shown: '5 km logged'}, and GET /api/artifacts/<reader>/db-grants lists the run log. Two runs: 00:42 +1 All tests passed, both. Before the fix (647958f22844) the same test failed: 'timed out waiting for the consent dialog's Allow armed (last seen: Allow disabled)' (reply e003b7a2).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PromptDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:31:44.788842Z","id":"3954d60bed09b589c6b9a460cf816f9be484608b942275f1bfb561d4779d3734","body":{"detail":"Failure: in app mode with requestAnimationFrame never calling back (the macOS app's WKWebView), a page that asks at load (claude.use('permissions').request(['comments']) needs no gesture, web/shell/src/caps/permissions.ts:14; a cross-app read on load asks too) opens the dialog before claxHost.init has run, or while claxHost.setVisible(false) holds. nextFrame(fn, true) decides once, at the call (web/shell/src/view/after-paint.ts:17), whether to start its fallback timer; shownByHost() is false then, no frame ever comes, and nothing restarts the wait when the host later says shown. Allow stays disabled for good: the failure of record fff04d3f again. Reproduced with a Playwright probe (requestAnimationFrame stubbed in every frame, a scratch daemon, a page that requests 'comments' on load, init and setVisible(true) called after the dialog showed): Allow disabled 4 s before init and still 4 s after; with init before the request it armed. The reverse also holds: a timer started while shown still arms Allow if the app is hidden before it fires, so Allow can be armed when the viewer returns without having seen the dialog. e2e/inter-app.spec.ts's no-frames test opens the dialog only after init, by a tap.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"44d1433759e4b67a092b6b9ad16f40c933f42840b2a1a4d472f62ea155e2199e"},"suggested_fix":"Make the whenShown wait follow the host's visibility: while shownByHost() is false keep only the frame request, and when the host turns shown (claxHost.init or setVisible(true), via a listener visibility.ts exposes) start the fallback then; when it turns hidden, cancel a pending fallback and disarm, counting ALLOW_DELAY_MS again from the next shown. Add a host test and an e2e case where the page asks at load, before init, with no frames.","summary":"A consent dialog opened before the app's init, or while the app says hidden, never arms Allow in a WebView that runs no frames","tags":["review","security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PromptDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:34:42.976644Z","id":"47d9dfdfe6ff670e5ae34ab76267e8cee5b01aad7f825ef64c4dc75279ee30c0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: PromptDialog's arming follows visibility.shown() through onHostVisibility: it restarts on each change of the host's word, and while the host says hidden Allow is disarmed. Evidence: shell/src/prompt.test.ts 'opened before the host's init, arms the delay after it says shown', 'hidden mid-delay does not arm, and counts the full delay again from the next shown' and 'opened while the host says hidden, arms only after it says shown' pass (rAF never fires); e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'with no animation frames, a permission dialog the page raised before the app's init arms once the app inits' passes; vitest 1558/1558. PromptDialog is the only whenShown user.","supersedes":"3954d60bed09b589c6b9a460cf816f9be484608b942275f1bfb561d4779d3734","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PromptDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:40:28.771315Z","id":"415dc35a7ce1cbf824a13ccc98eadc6f060dc07423a9b87e550e703f958ba66f","body":{"detail":"macOS debug app built from 647958f22844 with the embedded clax rebuilt (scripts/build-app-clax.sh macos), page reading document.visibilityState 'hidden'. The run log 23s940j6qrpv came from a replayed recorded result with one run added through the page (5.2 km, 1650 s). The dashboard pt64rxd9am1d was made by a live claude -p call (16.3 s; say-usable 17952 ms) declaring {\"db\":{\"read\":[\"23s940j6qrpv\"]}}. The consent dialog opened at once and armed Allow 0.7 s later; a real NSEvent click on Allow (pointer attested through claxHost) closed it. GET /api/artifacts/pt64rxd9am1d/db-grants lists {source_id: 23s940j6qrpv, granted_at: 2026-10-12T14:39:28.991Z}, and the dashboard renders 'This week, Oct 12 to Oct 18: 5.2 km, 27:30, 1 run, 5:17/km' with no further prompt.","kind":"comment","references":"1a48f8685e88fb6bb6695f5e248167f84edab7447f32737bd3227d0cd30b2d27","summary":"Confirmed live at 647958f22844: a claude -p dashboard's consent dialog arms and Allow grants the read","tags":["live-run","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/MoreMenu.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:40:26.000541Z","id":"db614cc3b79506e9884a54d693430ee9e338abc5815d144e2e79e20963acf6a8","body":{"detail":"On the app's transport (web/shell/src/transport.ts installTransport, onHost) the shell document's location is the app's shell origin (clax://app or https://app.clax.invalid), so ArtifactController.copyLink (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts copyLink, location.origin + here()) put an address on the clipboard that nothing outside the app can open, and Open raw (rawHref) opened the artifact's content-origin URL in a new window the app does not manage. The app's own bar has Share, which knows the artifact's real link.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"d3bc3cd558b1e51aaeeacdb8d60c91019ae2409efabc5a26de9a96a82c1e27e3"},"summary":"In the Clax app the more menu's Copy link copied an app-only address and Open raw opened a content-origin URL in a new window","tags":["review","app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/MoreMenu.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:44:56.580872Z","id":"5e02085b1e779602e6939433c2ba7dd2fdf5200425b3b09b82a79edb1d369c7d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f2284459b2440c3504082626f77bdacfae","summary":"Fixed: on the app's transport (onHost) MoreMenu renders neither Open raw nor Copy link and its wrapper takes .phone-only (hidden above 700 px, where its other items are bar buttons). bazelisk test //web:unit passed with topbar.test.ts 'in the Clax app the more menu has no Open raw or Copy link, and shows at phone width only' (browser: Versions, Open raw, Copy link; app: Versions), which failed before. Not yet checked in a WebView: web/e2e has no transport spec until plan Task 11.","supersedes":"db614cc3b79506e9884a54d693430ee9e338abc5815d144e2e79e20963acf6a8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:35:16.118159Z","id":"a7fbf613d189c7df3f2ac9419b55a82793ad7f02c4ffa051d7b0865fc3cc7d2a","body":{"detail":"A send with no live target makes untargeted feedback rows (clax-store feedback.rs send_in), which a watch hands over only to the owner's agents (routes/watches.rs put: retarget unless a grant), never to a person's agent. The dialog leaves the brief unsent and gives a prompt (view/new-artifact.ts connectPrompt) that tells the agent to watch the artifact and read the brief thread itself, which works for any harness.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"90da91d6418d5c30ebeb771373add25a228067e1f7bcab80c0fd58d74ddedaaf"},"summary":"With no agent live, send the brief untargeted so the first agent to watch takes it","tags":["revisit:agents following the prompt miss the brief","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:07:07.070362Z","id":"be60a87182f0bbcf711f2c8dd66055052d5cfa78dedd620d58aba98a1819b4f8","body":{"detail":"agents() (NewArtifactDialog.svelte:51-55) lists GET /api/agents (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs list_agents: every live agent, others' by name) through pickGroups (web/shell/src/view/new-artifact.ts:46-65), which filters only on live and a name. The send then refuses an agent that may not read the artifact (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs handoff_target -> named_agent_reaches: 400 agent_cannot_read) or may read but not watch (400 unknown_agent). On a hosted daemon a person invited without rights holds their own space only (crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs:4040, :5207), so when Mia starts an artifact while only Kim's agent is live, the dialog shows 'Kim's agents', every pick fails, and the poll at line 67 never ran (groups was non-empty), so the copyable connect prompt for Mia's own agent is never offered. The same holds for the owner's new artifact and any person's agent with rights narrowed to own or to named artifacts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"0b13bfa59f7ede8a2532f095fd6620d6e094eaf559477dd232af4032321e4cce"},"suggested_fix":"Offer only agents the send would reach: have the daemon answer the reachable agents for an artifact (or have GET /api/agents take ?artifact=<aid> and apply named_agent_reaches), and keep the connect prompt visible when the caller has no own agent among them.","summary":"The New dialog offers every live agent, including ones that may not read or watch the new artifact, and stops showing the connect prompt once any such agent is live","tags":["review","review:new-artifact","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:07:07.070517Z","id":"da736f3deee87a731ac1dac615caf6a4deb85c7f7b53f4c1f0937cc99ba62ec5","body":{"detail":"While busy, the header's Close (line 114), Cancel (line 124) and Escape (keydown line 100 -> close() -> onClose, since started is still null) unmount the dialog; the onMount cleanup (lines 42-47) clears poll while it is still undefined. create() then resumes: started is set, agents() runs, and with no live agent line 67 calls setInterval on the destroyed component. Nothing clears it until an agent connects or the page navigates, so the gallery polls GET /api/agents (and GET /api/viewers?ids=) every 3 s, and a second open of New adds another interval. The person also never lands on the artifact that was made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"905560aa1449ccd364efd59da7441d4826c820af52122749ede5294bb8e4817e"},"suggested_fix":"Track destruction (a flag set in the onMount cleanup, or an AbortController passed to start/liveAgents) and skip setting state and the interval after it; or disable Close, Cancel and Escape while busy, as the backdrop click already is.","summary":"Closing the dialog while Create is in flight leaves the artifact made and a 3 s /api/agents poll running with nothing to stop it","tags":["review","review:new-artifact","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:10:48.504378Z","id":"6f01582c8256c8bb12372e66cb792939e8b9d1047d13e75f0149b5c81f233a2b","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs:166-203 lists every roster session, pushing others' agents with only name/person/live and no reach check; web/shell/src/view/new-artifact.ts:46-61 pickGroups filters only on live and handle-or-name. The send (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:1222-1224 -> handoff_target :1318-1346 -> named_agent_reaches :504-545) answers 400 agent_cannot_read for a grant that cannot read the artifact and unknown_agent for one that may read but not watch. crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs:4040-4043 shows an invite without rights reads nothing but its own. web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte:67 polls only when groups is empty, and :136-158 shows the connect prompt only in the {:else} of groups.length, so with one unreachable live agent the prompt never appears.","kind":"comment","references":"be60a87182f0bbcf711f2c8dd66055052d5cfa78dedd620d58aba98a1819b4f8","summary":"confirmed: the dialog offers live agents the send would refuse, and a non-empty list hides the connect prompt","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:10:48.567101Z","id":"d4050c71eac52360251d4c52ccb7ae7c8a484918eeb827d3709414f95251dfef","body":{"detail":"NewArtifactDialog.svelte:114 (Close) and :124 (Cancel) call onClose directly, and :100 Escape -> close() :89 -> onClose while started is null; none checks busy (only the backdrop at :108 does). web/shell/src/ui/NewButton.svelte:26 unmounts the dialog on onClose. The cleanup at NewArtifactDialog.svelte:42-47 runs clearInterval(poll) with poll undefined; create() at :64-67 then resumes and, with no live agent, assigns poll = setInterval(...) that only clears itself when an agent appears. Minor: with no live agent liveAgents() returns [] so personNames (web/shell/src/view/new-artifact.ts:105-108) makes no /api/viewers request; the repeating poll is GET /api/agents.","kind":"comment","references":"da736f3deee87a731ac1dac615caf6a4deb85c7f7b53f4c1f0937cc99ba62ec5","summary":"confirmed: closing while Create is in flight leaves the made artifact unopened and starts an interval on the unmounted dialog","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:22.885635Z","id":"ca72f848554f7a83e966524c9f2e7bfbf7601a572e81d24b5067681d13527b13","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:565a3eb4c","summary":"Fixed: GET /api/agents?artifact=<aid> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs list_agents, may_send_at) lists only agents a send may name, applying named_agent_reaches and the caller's clax-comments send; the dialog lists that, reads it every 3 s and shows the connect prompt when it is empty. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__4 passes api_briefs::the_dialog_lists_and_a_send_reaches_only_agents_that_may_read_and_watch (Lee's unreadable and Kim's unwatchable agents left out, reader gets []) and //crates/clax-server:integration__1 passes api_hosted::a_member_who_may_not_send_attaches_no_agent_and_agent_tokens_start_nothing; //web:unit passes.","supersedes":"be60a87182f0bbcf711f2c8dd66055052d5cfa78dedd620d58aba98a1819b4f8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:22.978906Z","id":"27ea13763f497e07867b30b40d762a9d26439356d02b559fb1caafcf0a0086fd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6afa41ec1","summary":"Fixed: the dialog tracks destroyed (set in the onMount cleanup); a Create that answers after unmount lands on the artifact (nav.assign) and sets no state and starts no interval; the interval is cleared on destroy. Evidence: //web:unit passes new-artifact.test.ts 'closed while Create is in flight, lands on the artifact made and polls nothing' (setInterval never called, no /api/agents request, assign('/a/abc')).","supersedes":"da736f3deee87a731ac1dac615caf6a4deb85c7f7b53f4c1f0937cc99ba62ec5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:06:41.267117Z","id":"483c5759436b5831a673bf8b2bc783c2ba59ef356e1cf6329c6232fa4a8161ab","body":{"detail":"The floating window's box rules live in DrawerChrome.svelte (lazy) to keep the artifact entry under its bundle budget, so SidebarIsland skips the placeholder while data-drawer is float. Wider than a phone nothing moves (a floating drawer takes no room from the page); at phone width, a Threads tap before the chunk arrives shows the page a moment longer instead of an empty sheet. The chunk is prefetched after the first paint (web/shell/src/ui/sidebar-chunk.ts), so the window is short.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"d07f0934061a48b3afd66055531666c8b4e25cb2887e59068f75bc432d5a4a75"},"summary":"With the drawer set to float, no empty sidebar is drawn before the thread list's chunk loads, at phone width too","tags":["revisit:the artifact entry's budget is raised","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:06:41.267190Z","id":"b0bc7c9552ce6aa52ed2b76137eaf7c66168583c8466fa488f05dd4676a52973","body":{"detail":"The bottom dock keeps the sidebar's single column (cards span the viewer's width), the least change to Sidebar.svelte, which the extension's panel shares. A multi-column flow would read better on wide screens but changes the sidebar's section and tail layout.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"2c6cbe71232d9aafe5941effa5fe8e9d27e0564247f5b6f806c71664d27a8c17"},"summary":"Docked at the bottom, the thread cards could flow in columns across the strip instead of one full-width list","tags":["revisit:people use the bottom dock on wide screens and find the cards too wide","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/drawer.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:15:40.530079Z","id":"1895e8b990debb48df4cdd5fcc9b23562717e01391ced86ca6c1d0eac9b5bbf8","body":{"detail":"drawer.svelte.ts:7 sets `prefs = normal(readPrefs())` but calls applyPrefs only inside `set` (line 14), so whatever the head script (web/shell/artifact.html:7) put on the root stays until the viewer changes something. normal() (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.ts:59-69) caps w at 720 and drops float coordinates unless all four are numbers, but the CSS (SidebarIsland.svelte:61, DrawerChrome.svelte:153-155) caps the docked width only at the viewer less 320 px. Failure: clax.drawer = {\"layout\":\"right\",\"w\":5000} at 1440 px shows a 1120 px drawer whose separator announces aria-valuenow 1120 with aria-valuemax 720 (sizeOf, drawer-model.ts:137); {\"layout\":\"float\",\"x\":900} places the window by --drawer-x while the model holds no place. The Infinity case in the head script (artifact.html:7) persists the same way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"92c471b825b4ba6bfb30872685cdad10500badaaa6a5becf817598aa34a1d5b5"},"suggested_fix":"Call applyPrefs(prefs) once when drawer.svelte.ts loads (it is in the lazy chunk, so the artifact entry's budget is untouched), or write `normal`'s result back with drawer.set(prefs, false).","summary":"The checked prefs are never applied: the head script's unchecked values stay on the root until the first move or resize","tags":["review","review:drawer-layout","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:15:40.530132Z","id":"36ab259899ced9ccc524c14e7960a6446c14a039fb6c8cd8dc17c21310bea863","body":{"detail":"The window defaults to the viewer's top right, 16 px in, full height less 32 px, at z-index 3. Pins sit at their heading's top right, kept off the stage's right edge (web/shell/src/ui/Pins.svelte:71, theme.css:201-202, no z-index), so on any page whose headings span the stage every pin is under the window: target/drawer-shots/light-desktop-float.png shows the pin for thread 3 at about (1412, 78) hidden but for its top rim. The composer (theme.css:206, right 16 px, bottom 16 px, z-index 5) and .stage-foot (theme.css:179, z-index 4) are drawn above the window, so while composing they cover its corner grip and the last thread's Reply row. Failure: 1440x900, Float threads over the page, then try to click a pin or press Comment and resize the window by its corner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"20b58f39e19b677ce3bb66b37257c62daec39fff2c1486b37cd3386defcf7043"},"suggested_fix":"Default the window's x clear of the pin column (for example 48 px in from the right), and either raise the window above .stage-foot and the composer or keep the composer's box out of the window's (e.g. place the composer to the window's left while floating).","summary":"The floating window's default place covers the stage's pin column, and the composer and stage-foot banners draw over its bottom right","tags":["review","review:drawer-layout","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:15:40.530168Z","id":"2f33e1cf040bef87a0e096a8b3ed6bdd9b06acf1f44a7996857e35dc58b1a1a1","body":{"detail":"onClose is ctl.togglePanel() (web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte:39), which sets panel false (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:1532); SidebarIsland.svelte:40-43 then unmounts the drawer that holds the focused Hide threads button, and nothing moves focus. Failure: Tab to Hide threads, press Enter: focus lands on <body>, so the next Tab starts again at the top bar's Gallery link instead of at the Threads button that reopens the drawer (WCAG 2.4.3 Focus Order, https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/focus-order.html).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"ded8e09ad083adc4d37d8d8a0a7621b50e440008cd8eb3eb5bd69f16394b40f2"},"suggested_fix":"After closing, focus the top bar's Threads toggle (web/shell/src/ui/TopbarIsland.svelte:65), e.g. by passing a focus target through onClose.","summary":"Hide threads removes the focused button with the drawer, dropping keyboard focus to the document body","tags":["review","review:drawer-layout","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:15:40.530199Z","id":"bad66133a5ac690ceb419599951abe66e5d655f336f986e37cb04262411259a7","body":{"detail":"drag() listens for pointerup, pointercancel and lostpointercapture on the captured element `t` only. Per Pointer Events, when the capture target is no longer connected the lostpointercapture event is fired at the Document, not at the element (https://www.w3.org/TR/pointerevents3/#implicit-release-of-pointer-capture), so if the drawer unmounts mid-drag (the view leaving viewReady, SidebarIsland.svelte:37) `end` never runs and `.viewer.drawer-drag .stage *` keeps pointer-events: none (DrawerChrome.svelte:186): the frame and pins take no pointer until a reload. Escape during a drag does nothing; the move is kept and stored on release, with no way back to `from`.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":81},"content_hash":"9108fdfeac602648c0f9775f26fce3c8c89bec69f254814f3bc9e9d9c6fa55be"},"suggested_fix":"While dragging, also listen on the document for lostpointercapture and keydown Escape (Escape: drawer.set(from) and end), and clear .drawer-drag in the component's teardown.","summary":"A drag cannot be cancelled with Escape, and it ends only by events on the handle, so a handle removed mid-drag leaves .drawer-drag on the viewer","tags":["review","review:drawer-layout","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:15:40.530238Z","id":"221fb55b834a1a4afd95f95f520afbeee11dad486e7f1a8180d8f20d8773e628","body":{"detail":"`order: -1` moves the drawer to the left visually only; in the DOM it stays after .stage (web/shell/src/view/skeleton.ts:8), so Tab goes top bar, pins and frame, then the drawer's bar and threads. CSS order does not change focus order (https://www.w3.org/TR/css-flexbox-1/#order-accessibility), while SidebarIsland.svelte:3-4 states the island's aim that Tab follows the screen. Failure: Dock threads left, Tab from the top bar: focus enters the page on the right before the threads on the left.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":62},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"c31ddb131f2cb67143b70daae0b8aa3d49a8f15118f2c53b8c909b2734708545"},"suggested_fix":"Accept and record it as a waiver, or render the drawer island before the stage when docked left.","summary":"Docked left, the drawer is drawn before the page but reached by Tab after it","tags":["review","review:drawer-layout","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:18:25.686212Z","id":"60b5a0d3a7c087e1448aee2ec68cfb2662ec9d501e3c9a3c0670df0bd281c1bc","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte:67-80: `end` is registered only on the captured element `t` (pointerup, pointercancel, lostpointercapture). Nothing listens for keydown during a drag, and no $effect teardown removes `drawer-drag`, which lives on the skeleton's .viewer (web/shell/src/view/skeleton.ts:8). That element outlives the component, so if the handle is removed mid-drag, `.viewer.drawer-drag .stage *` keeps `pointer-events: none !important` (line 186). Removing the handle mid-drag is uncommon (it needs the view or panel state to change while the pointer is held), so the finding is rightly a suggestion.","kind":"comment","references":"bad66133a5ac690ceb419599951abe66e5d655f336f986e37cb04262411259a7","summary":"confirmed: a drag ends only by events on the handle, has no Escape and no teardown","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:18:25.686408Z","id":"2a98c46cf998f1881d72256c6e92d60a15fe6d305cf9a4ba6235e8aa0c41d27f","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte:39 passes onClose={() => ctl.togglePanel()}, and web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:1532 flips panel. SidebarIsland.svelte:40-43 then drops <Sidebar> (and with it DrawerChrome and its button). No focus() call exists in DrawerChrome.svelte, ShellSidebar.svelte, SidebarIsland.svelte or TopbarIsland.svelte (grep). One correction: Chromium and Firefox keep the sequential focus navigation starting point where the removed node was, so the next Tab may continue after the drawer's position rather than at the Gallery link. Focus still lands on <body> and does not return to the Threads toggle (TopbarIsland.svelte:65), so the concern stands.","kind":"comment","references":"2f33e1cf040bef87a0e096a8b3ed6bdd9b06acf1f44a7996857e35dc58b1a1a1","summary":"confirmed: Hide threads unmounts the focused button and nothing moves focus","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:18:25.686600Z","id":"74f90d43abf1beea789f1298c123b0e0200207d2350eccce31292157410974d5","body":{"detail":"DrawerChrome.svelte:153-155 places the window at `100% - var(--fw) - 16px`, top 16px, height `100% - 32px`, z-index 3, absolute in .viewer. .stage (web/shell/src/theme.css:186) is position: relative with no z-index, so it makes no stacking context. Its .pins (theme.css:199, no z-index) paint under the window, while .composer (theme.css:206, right/bottom 16px, z-index 5) and .stage-foot (theme.css:179, z-index 4) paint over it. The composer's box therefore sits exactly on the window's bottom-right corner, where the corner grip is (DrawerChrome.svelte:175). In target/drawer-shots/light-desktop-float.png only the top rim of the red pin shows, at about (1412, 75), above the window's border.","kind":"comment","references":"36ab259899ced9ccc524c14e7960a6446c14a039fb6c8cd8dc17c21310bea863","summary":"confirmed: the default floating window hides top-right pins, and the composer and stage foot paint over its corner","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:18:25.686773Z","id":"ad2ba5788b2976280d8d79a649912026a1f29c0e1cb816f8af5dce6a1d10d523","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte:62 uses `[data-drawer=\"left\"] .drawer { order: -1; }`. The sidebar island is the .viewer's last child, after .stage (web/shell/src/view/skeleton.ts:8; web/shell/artifact.html body). CSS Flexbox 1 §5.4.1 (https://www.w3.org/TR/css-flexbox-1/#order-accessibility) says `order` does not affect sequential navigation. The island's own comment (SidebarIsland.svelte:3-4) aims for Tab to follow the screen. Kind suggestion fits.","kind":"comment","references":"221fb55b834a1a4afd95f95f520afbeee11dad486e7f1a8180d8f20d8773e628","summary":"confirmed: docked left, the drawer is moved only visually, and Tab still reaches it after the page","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/drawer.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:18:25.686940Z","id":"bfa248a0b1cb2d94b4b1145209f5514e2e3c60ee7e4c3c5fac263b0ed3fc946e","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/drawer.svelte.ts:7 sets prefs = normal(readPrefs()), and applyPrefs is called only in set (line 14). grep finds no other applyPrefs caller in web/shell/src outside tests, and every drawer.set call is a user action (DrawerChrome.svelte:64,75,89,92,106,135). For {\"layout\":\"right\",\"w\":5000} the head script sets --drawer-w:5000px, and SidebarIsland.svelte:61 yields min(5000px, 100% - 320px). sizeOf (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.ts:137) reports now = the measured box width and max = min(720, view.w - 320), so now exceeds max. For {\"layout\":\"float\",\"x\":900}, --drawer-x drives `left` (DrawerChrome.svelte:155), while normal() (drawer-model.ts:65) keeps no place.","kind":"comment","references":"1895e8b990debb48df4cdd5fcc9b23562717e01391ced86ca6c1d0eac9b5bbf8","summary":"confirmed: normal(readPrefs()) is never applied, so the head script's unchecked values stay on the root","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/drawer.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:40:58.530126Z","id":"e692a8e0a0fdd612a6476d289c04e9ba1ccfd24dedc3e1de641b79bf7c24ac01","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0c0bec1a6","summary":"drawer.svelte.ts applies normal(readPrefs()) to the root as it loads. Evidence: web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.test.ts 'are checked and laid out again once the drawer's controls load, over what the head script applied' (stored {\"layout\":\"float\",\"w\":5000,\"h\":3,\"x\":900} over a root carrying --drawer-w:5000px and --drawer-x:900px ends with --drawer-w:720px, --drawer-h:160px and no --drawer-x) passes: bazelisk test //web:unit, 1741 passed.","supersedes":"1895e8b990debb48df4cdd5fcc9b23562717e01391ced86ca6c1d0eac9b5bbf8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:40:59.004821Z","id":"f942760045360dbdc9201090a3c7a2a3aba99f49d295d59639b3bd890eb1f0b1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:547a204d7","summary":"The floating window defaults to 48 px in from the right (pins keep PIN_RIGHT_ROOM, 38 px, off the stage's edge), is drawn at z-index 6 above the composer (5) and .stage-foot (4), and those keep to the stage's room beside it through --float-clear-left/right, which the drawer's controls measure. Evidence: web/e2e/drawer.spec.ts 'floating, the window leaves the pins clear by default, and the composer keeps beside it with the window's grip reachable' (pin box clear of the window; composer box clear of it, the corner grip and the composer's textarea topmost at their centres; moved left, the composer returns to the right) passes in bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest with drawer.spec.ts and echo.spec.ts, 17 passed; target/drawer-shots/{light,dark}-desktop-float.png show the pin beside the window.","supersedes":"36ab259899ced9ccc524c14e7960a6446c14a039fb6c8cd8dc17c21310bea863","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:40:59.315129Z","id":"4b291a9ea0abe6295bdabad7fbafce08686e30488ba4448de2db29402f3147be","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:194c079c7","summary":"Hide threads now focuses the top bar's Threads toggle once the drawer has closed. Evidence: web/e2e/drawer.spec.ts 'docked right by default, …' focuses Hide threads, presses Enter, expects .topbar button.threads focused, presses Enter and sees the drawer again; passes in bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest (drawer.spec.ts and echo.spec.ts, 17 passed).","supersedes":"2f33e1cf040bef87a0e096a8b3ed6bdd9b06acf1f44a7996857e35dc58b1a1a1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/DrawerChrome.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:40:59.541421Z","id":"b1a01fba5e6498e6309049ea2541fef60d8b15d6f6f64d205bc0ece8a4f529d8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6a84913df","summary":"A drag listens on the document (capture) for pointermove, pointerup, pointercancel, lostpointercapture and Escape, ends once, ends when the drawer unmounts, and Escape puts the drawer back where the drag began. Evidence: web/e2e/drawer.spec.ts 'docked right by default, …' presses Escape mid-drag (width back to 392, .drawer-drag gone, nothing stored after release) and removes the handle mid-drag (.drawer-drag gone, the page takes the pointer); passes in bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest, 17 passed.","supersedes":"bad66133a5ac690ceb419599951abe66e5d655f336f986e37cb04262411259a7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:41:00.131864Z","id":"c130a27d08f3f90bdc8701907be9ef3b363a2da67abf9977c78737e531ea1345","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5b1fcf434","summary":"Docked left wider than a phone, DrawerChrome.svelte moves the sidebar's island before the stage (the stage and frame stay), back after it otherwise and on unmount, keeping focus inside the drawer. Evidence: web/e2e/drawer.spec.ts 'docked left, then at the bottom, …' checks Tab from the top bar's last button reaches the page when docked right and at the bottom and the drawer when docked left, the drawer precedes .stage in the DOM, and the layout button keeps focus; passes in bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest, 17 passed.","supersedes":"221fb55b834a1a4afd95f95f520afbeee11dad486e7f1a8180d8f20d8773e628","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Markdown.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:28:58.613279Z","id":"cffe54a5cadc63e1d14930e38d95040caef804df0beffe0168e4cd07fcd703a9","body":{"detail":"`<input type=\"checkbox\" disabled checked={...} />` sits beside the item's text with no `<label>`, `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`, so a screen reader announces an unnamed, dimmed checkbox and reads the item's text as a separate node. Being `disabled` also takes it out of the focus order, so a keyboard user does not reach its state at all.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"15cac05494c2c542adc03d8e43ffe53362b19198ea1046aa490ccb1064c0d7ed"},"suggested_fix":"Name it by its item (an id on the item's first block and `aria-labelledby`), or wrap box and text in a `<label>`; consider `aria-readonly` styling instead of `disabled` if the state should be reachable.","summary":"A task item's checkbox has no accessible name","tags":["review","review:comment-markdown-115cb94","a11y","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Markdown.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:30:45.671355Z","id":"01b8a1f300e2e135788342b879b37b1488654bbf6e2dfa42cdb6e28a83331dd0","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/Markdown.svelte:27 renders `<input type=\"checkbox\" disabled checked={it.checked} />` with no label, aria-label or aria-labelledby; `grep -n \"aria-label\\|<label\" web/shell/src/ui/Markdown.svelte` prints nothing. A disabled input is removed from sequential focus (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#enabling-and-disabling-form-controls:-the-disabled-attribute).","kind":"comment","references":"cffe54a5cadc63e1d14930e38d95040caef804df0beffe0168e4cd07fcd703a9","summary":"confirmed: the task checkbox has no accessible name and is disabled","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Markdown.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:50:00.816105Z","id":"2d5b14b863b8fdc48fc9a1dc5db655081f87752e5640c4d75ae7b5ce27ab2a2a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ea4bd31da","summary":"Fixed in ea4bd31da: the read-only box carries aria-label \"done\" or \"not done\" beside its checked state; it stays out of the focus order. markdown.test.ts \"reads lists ... task lists with read-only boxes\" checks the labels; `bazelisk test //web:unit` passed at 7a1df0ce2.","supersedes":"cffe54a5cadc63e1d14930e38d95040caef804df0beffe0168e4cd07fcd703a9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:10.232085Z","id":"ece44c9f518e61ca5f13ba4b6a346c843d0fd48ef3deb0c78a42c8eca90cce36","body":{"detail":"A send with no live target makes untargeted feedback rows (clax-store feedback.rs send_in), which a watch hands over only to the owner's agents (routes/watches.rs put: retarget unless a grant), never to a person's agent. The dialog leaves the brief unsent and gives a prompt (view/new-artifact.ts connectPrompt) that tells the agent to watch the artifact and read the brief thread itself, which works for any harness.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"047fbfdb6a9cb6821810e911b198969f5f50130f1041d6f763455778dcdbf36d"},"summary":"With no agent live, send the brief untargeted so the first agent to watch takes it","supersedes":"a7fbf613d189c7df3f2ac9419b55a82793ad7f02c4ffa051d7b0865fc3cc7d2a","tags":["revisit:agents following the prompt miss the brief","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:19.533544Z","id":"1640024047cf88100b7138db27bc5b653dc13dd8fc23bdc83f7636686cbc5106","body":{"detail":"The gallery loads every artifact the viewer sees once and filters in the browser, by name or ID without case (web/shell/src/view/tags-model.ts carriesAll), as the search does, so pressing a tag needs no request and the tag bar can list every tag in use. The daemon's ?tag= filter (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs list) matches the same way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":125},"content_hash":"b2fff55d9c303464d4653c2eec552e73a69e8a3381a4c7323c1d0755ef2bddec"},"summary":"Filter the gallery by tag through GET /api/artifacts?tag= instead of over the list it has loaded","tags":["tags","revisit:the gallery stops loading every artifact at once (paging)","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:19.533624Z","id":"9f2a156eb88a225cfd93dffac51f1dd288472873468209a3c77e2d1683ca9b50","body":{"detail":"A tag filter shows one list, pinned first then most recent, as a search does: the filter is a narrowing the viewer chose, and sections of two or three cards read as noise. The bar's pressed tags say what is shown.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":125},"content_hash":"b2fff55d9c303464d4653c2eec552e73a69e8a3381a4c7323c1d0755ef2bddec"},"summary":"Keep the gallery's attention sections (Needs your eyes, Everything else) under a tag filter","tags":["tags","revisit:owners ask to see what needs them within a tag","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:19.535936Z","id":"7934d6b0144843ee12002b94d732c3532977fdc4e3c5f034ce3a6b0f6e87faca","body":{"detail":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs measures the People page's chunk (people) but not the Tags page's (TagsPage.svelte, TagForm.svelte) nor the tag editor's (ui/tag-editor.ts, TagPicker.svelte); they load lazily, and nothing gates their growth.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"072f176dcb6a9779cf4f51498c3d90137d12e01615db042a6043bd239a076887"},"summary":"The Tags page's chunk has no bundle-size measure","tags":["tags","bundle","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagEditor.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:19.535985Z","id":"8edb3d8c76f7a275ae667f146107b9200b8c3de7e3be09ace03803b61343907f","body":{"detail":"Each check sends PATCH /api/artifacts/<id>/tags {add|remove} at once, so a second viewer sees it live and nothing is lost when the popover closes by a press outside. A PUT on close would send one request and one tags event for several changes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"bb480c7e151f2bdb31d14de80fd06dd869c889d1ef977a3f9c669cee8ef2c6da"},"summary":"Apply the artifact's tags in one PUT when the editor closes instead of a PATCH per box checked","tags":["tags","revisit:people tag many artifacts with many tags at once","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagEditor.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:48.598332Z","id":"224754163155e2ec6e9616303b89668a3a2b69cbbf81a71093953595a16496a6","body":{"detail":"toggle() returns at once while busy (line 32). TagPicker's onchange (TagPicker.svelte:48) awaits that immediate return and sets box.checked = chosen(t), which is still false, so the viewer's second check flips back with no message and no request. Checking two tags quickly (or Space twice on adjacent boxes) on a slow link applies only the first. The Enter path (TagPicker.svelte:28) is dropped the same way. No unit test covers TagEditor (tag-picker.test.ts mounts TagPicker with a stub onToggle).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"6ac86ee7552b48c38901a21e92ea5813b3546b4ab70aea9d46ee8b5dab610b77"},"suggested_fix":"Queue toggles (chain each PATCH on the previous promise) instead of dropping them, or disable the boxes while busy so the refusal is visible; add a TagEditor test with a held first response.","summary":"A second check made while the first PATCH is in flight is dropped silently and its box unchecks","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags-ui","tags","artifact-page","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:48.598495Z","id":"80ce627cc8c8e6c42d978455f7f89c2eb082fbbfbe287453e5627c39747654f3","body":{"detail":"remove() sets error = \"Could not delete …\" in its catch and then awaits load(), whose success handler sets error = null (line 25). A delete refused by the daemon (403 owner_only, a 404 because another page deleted it first, a network blip that recovers) therefore shows nothing: the alert flashes for one fetch and the tag stays in the list with no explanation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"be989d83986f549903d335f4f19323c906ac759db9959b6e6b011ddac75f9571"},"suggested_fix":"Keep load errors and action errors apart (a loadError and an actionError), or clear error only on a new action, not on a successful reload.","summary":"A failed delete's message is erased at once by the reload that follows it","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags-ui","tags","tags-page","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:48.598530Z","id":"39b3386fe7c49d6fe1af86f51f54f815c9aae64c0f013ecd87fe3f86bfb1b2d0","body":{"detail":"Edit and New tag open TagForm and focus its Name field (TagForm.svelte:32); Save (line 39), Cancel and Escape (TagForm.svelte:31) set editing = null, which unmounts the form, and nothing moves focus back to the row's Edit button or to New tag. A keyboard or screen-reader user is returned to the top of the document after every edit. The artifact page's tag editor returns focus to its button on Escape (ui/tag-editor.ts:43); this page does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"13c4338de846f6d79889ba53d872101a78d3bc27ced8e68def5e091de09b57fd"},"suggested_fix":"Remember the button that opened the form and focus it (or the saved row's tag link) after the form closes, in a tick.","summary":"Saving or cancelling a tag's form drops keyboard focus to the page body","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags-ui","tags","tags-page","a11y","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:48.598557Z","id":"7ad0f57f3d382ce5525c1793fd7384d27cbb2189f8012e363954d704a69634f7","body":{"detail":"The subtitle for !may_manage is \"You can put these tags on the artifacts you made.\" It shows to a hosted guest or a LAN viewer (Caller::Viewer), whom clax_http::agent::administers refuses for every artifact (agent.rs:961), so the sentence is false for them; only a signed-in person (or their agents) administers artifacts they made.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":69},"content_hash":"7e7f180bae4ebf3923c4533ed4d45773f77e6ae63698be30de4646cd5e13eef5"},"suggested_fix":"Say it only to a signed-in person (the viewer from /api/viewers/me), and otherwise only that the owner keeps the list.","summary":"The Tags page tells every non-manager they can put tags on the artifacts they made","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags-ui","tags","tags-page","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:48.598598Z","id":"fbb35fd6a1eb7df677719565870faa978a9f5c31d6af6719f705f194648dc345","body":{"detail":"The filter keeps names (sel, ?tag=name). When the owner renames q4 to \"Q4 plan\", the tags event refetches the cards (card-sync.ts:52) and carriesAll no longer matches: the gallery says \"No artifacts carry every tag chosen.\" and the bar shows a grey \"q4\" chip (tags-model.ts barTags) beside the new \"Q4 plan\". The viewer has to take q4 out and press Q4 plan. Deleting a selected tag does the same, which is expected; a rename is not a change the viewer made.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"445aa0c80d3d863432d0e982c583ba9c6bc46db40114b10b76dbef07173a4d54"},"suggested_fix":"On a tags event with the list loaded, map each selected name to the ID it named before and rewrite sel (and the address, with replaceState) to the tag's new name.","summary":"A tag renamed or deleted while it filters the gallery leaves an empty gallery under its old name","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags-ui","tags","gallery","live","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:40:53.413686Z","id":"7d9c07efda0b0c030aa873d9eafa3a6493bea3dffde756b2ceb834b0c950e234","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte:69 keeps sel as names from ?tag=, and :121 filters by carriesAll(a, sel); web/shell/src/view/tags-model.ts:14 matches a ref by ID or folded name. Nothing rewrites sel on a tags event (web/shell/src/ui/card-sync.ts:50-51 only refetches cards). node --experimental-strip-types over a copy of tags-model.ts: carriesAll({tags:[{id:'t_abc123',name:'Q4 plan'}]}, ['q4']) -> false, so the card drops out and barTags adds a grey 'q4' chip.","kind":"comment","references":"fbb35fd6a1eb7df677719565870faa978a9f5c31d6af6719f705f194648dc345","summary":"confirmed: the gallery filter holds tag names, so a rename of a selected tag empties the filtered gallery","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagEditor.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:40:53.413864Z","id":"a75de8e9fda03de1d1dadf79f7c492abec6c4671e26052cb6f48756f594f9e8a","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/TagEditor.svelte:32 `if (busy) return;` with no message; web/shell/src/ui/TagPicker.svelte:48 awaits onToggle then sets box.checked = p.chosen(t), which is still the pre-change value, so the second check unchecks silently. The Enter path (TagPicker.svelte:28) calls the same toggle. No test mounts TagEditor (grep for TagEditor in test files finds none).","kind":"comment","references":"224754163155e2ec6e9616303b89668a3a2b69cbbf81a71093953595a16496a6","summary":"confirmed: a toggle during an in-flight PATCH returns at once and TagPicker resets the box to its old state","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:40:53.414041Z","id":"d133745e3a54dedac9536bf5d7827320c10d56a3e2bc9e58404a0fdeb8b54db6","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte:50 sets error in the catch, :52 then awaits load(), and load's success handler (:25) sets error = null. Any refused delete whose list reload succeeds ends with no alert shown.","kind":"comment","references":"80ce627cc8c8e6c42d978455f7f89c2eb082fbbfbe287453e5627c39747654f3","summary":"confirmed: remove()'s error is cleared by the load() that follows it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:40:53.414217Z","id":"3e7e0c055d3afed45a70babe59e756046cc1256d3816dc0fd3c0c8d5b2dbd8a6","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte:69 shows 'You can put these tags on the artifacts you made.' whenever !may_manage. crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:961 returns false for Caller::Viewer and Caller::Anonymous, and web/e2e/tags.spec.ts:146-158 shows a LAN viewer does load /tags. One part of the detail does not hold: a hosted guest never sees this page, since crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1174 maps GET /tags to GuestNeed::Gallery and :1632 redirects it to /signin. The LAN case suffices for the claim.","kind":"comment","references":"7ad0f57f3d382ce5525c1793fd7384d27cbb2189f8012e363954d704a69634f7","summary":"confirmed: the non-manager subtitle is false for a LAN viewer, who administers no artifact","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:40:53.414395Z","id":"7728820b5a81462b4c86f33be41f1ae1da0b6357db0bbf7fb21513bdd68ae9cb","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte:39 (save) and the onCancel handlers at :72 and :78 set editing = null, unmounting TagForm, which had focused its Name field (web/shell/src/ui/TagForm.svelte:32); Escape calls onCancel (TagForm.svelte:31). No code in TagsPage.svelte calls focus() afterwards, unlike web/shell/src/ui/tag-editor.ts:41, which refocuses its button.","kind":"comment","references":"39b3386fe7c49d6fe1af86f51f54f815c9aae64c0f013ecd87fe3f86bfb1b2d0","summary":"confirmed: closing the tag form unmounts it with no focus restored","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:08:48.728804Z","id":"e250f8a04b886593612df8cd20bd09c8a7053a81c50d0ddb680324e1362b08f6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cfb4688dd","summary":"Fixed: the gallery holds its filter by ID, rewrites the address's names in place on a rename (replaceState, history length unchanged) and drops a deleted tag after refetching the whole list on the tags event; tags.spec.ts 'a second page follows tag changes live…' expects ?tag=Q4+plan&tag=design after the rename and ?tag=Q4+plan after deleting design (//web:e2e_rest tags.spec.ts inbox.spec.ts: 8 passed)","supersedes":"fbb35fd6a1eb7df677719565870faa978a9f5c31d6af6719f705f194648dc345","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagEditor.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:08:48.833359Z","id":"0f89b3ce86517f8467b3ea2994a747819148346743b1faaadfdc1271a56cdc43","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2255a0f67","summary":"Fixed: each toggle records the state asked (shown at once) and is chained after the ones before it, so none is dropped and Enter in the search acts the same way; tag-editor.test.ts 'sends each change in turn, losing none made while one is on its way' clicks two boxes during one PATCH and sees both sent in order and both checked (bazelisk test //web:unit passes)","supersedes":"224754163155e2ec6e9616303b89668a3a2b69cbbf81a71093953595a16496a6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:08:48.886223Z","id":"e12b519dbf77886002ede3c9872a768fdd584e0942836a1d9e2253d03539cf19","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:17ad33396","summary":"Fixed: a load error and an action's refusal are kept apart, so the reload after a refused delete no longer clears it; gallery.test.ts 'is the Tags page at /tags…' answers DELETE with 404 and still reads 'Could not delete Q4: no such tag' after the reload (bazelisk test //web:unit passes)","supersedes":"80ce627cc8c8e6c42d978455f7f89c2eb082fbbfbe287453e5627c39747654f3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:08:48.913465Z","id":"dc2f6714c288c06b81c12e5a80753e4015d4e8b965ea5aed51a1806d75848434","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:17ad33396","summary":"Fixed: closeForm returns focus to the row's Edit button or New tag, and a delete to the row now in its place; tags.spec.ts checks New tag focused after Create and after Cancel, Edit tag q4 after Escape, and Edit tag Q4 plan after deleting design (//web:e2e_rest tags.spec.ts inbox.spec.ts: 8 passed)","supersedes":"39b3386fe7c49d6fe1af86f51f54f815c9aae64c0f013ecd87fe3f86bfb1b2d0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagsPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:08:48.939582Z","id":"cbe803a852d54009286a6672d2c8ad7bf434bbe1db3218cd573a4a12a4ddbca0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:17ad33396","summary":"Fixed: the line under the heading reads may_manage, else GET /api/viewers/me may_create: 'You can put these tags on the artifacts you made.' only for a viewer who makes artifacts, else 'The owner keeps this list.'; gallery.test.ts checks the reader's line and hosted.spec.ts the member's (//web:unit passes; hosted.spec.ts 9 passed)","supersedes":"7ad0f57f3d382ce5525c1793fd7384d27cbb2189f8012e363954d704a69634f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/card-sync.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:02.447674Z","id":"d7037e1634b9abb399590f8512df7a557ac607b9675569592dd14052fd82fb24","body":{"detail":"The gallery topic is shared by every viewer, so it cannot carry this viewer's attention (addressed threads, new replies, open threads): a version, thread or thread_deleted event there still fetches the viewer's attention on that one artifact, and a card's roster (participants) is only as fresh as the last full fetch (going live, resync, and every SAFETY_MS).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"7bdd3932434a71d1ad19e2be45e3bcc78fc1aeb1b9b1eb6f901e3465908a0ac1"},"suggested_fix":"A per-viewer topic, or attention computed from the thread summary, would remove the fetch.","summary":"The gallery fetches this viewer's attention per event","supersedes":"487dd91624f77a276deb8f3ecfe7963392c43620da67d0e2082724611e817b40","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:02.658083Z","id":"3bc02bcacc4f6216fef2eba072f6283881bf93310abbfa65ff65a3a03faee8ce","body":{"detail":"The gallery loads every artifact the viewer sees once and filters in the browser, by name or ID without case (web/shell/src/view/tags-model.ts carriesAll), as the search does, so pressing a tag needs no request and the tag bar can list every tag in use. The daemon's ?tag= filter (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs list) matches the same way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"b2fff55d9c303464d4653c2eec552e73a69e8a3381a4c7323c1d0755ef2bddec"},"summary":"Filter the gallery by tag through GET /api/artifacts?tag= instead of over the list it has loaded","supersedes":"1640024047cf88100b7138db27bc5b653dc13dd8fc23bdc83f7636686cbc5106","tags":["tags","revisit:the gallery stops loading every artifact at once (paging)","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:02.865318Z","id":"e1e1e6204c83c759c87c49c3a87feb1e760c81ba0e259721bf8cd2607a4463fb","body":{"detail":"A tag filter shows one list, pinned first then most recent, as a search does: the filter is a narrowing the viewer chose, and sections of two or three cards read as noise. The bar's pressed tags say what is shown.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"b2fff55d9c303464d4653c2eec552e73a69e8a3381a4c7323c1d0755ef2bddec"},"summary":"Keep the gallery's attention sections (Needs your eyes, Everything else) under a tag filter","supersedes":"9f2a156eb88a225cfd93dffac51f1dd288472873468209a3c77e2d1683ca9b50","tags":["tags","revisit:owners ask to see what needs them within a tag","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TagEditor.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:03.996762Z","id":"8bf30e7eada494e69a7bbcb3c577741127b6292ca2841dadbec60515f5ab2805","body":{"detail":"Each check sends PATCH /api/artifacts/<id>/tags {add|remove} at once, so a second viewer sees it live and nothing is lost when the popover closes by a press outside. A PUT on close would send one request and one tags event for several changes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"4297ee4122f55ca1335d8c2a94a4edf871adb9bd80fd7d60a567394fef244d00"},"summary":"Apply the artifact's tags in one PUT when the editor closes instead of a PATCH per box checked","supersedes":"8edb3d8c76f7a275ae667f146107b9200b8c3de7e3be09ace03803b61343907f","tags":["tags","revisit:people tag many artifacts with many tags at once","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:39:50.649623Z","id":"7a30c815cf44f6ba4f5d4651d2ffe94321b576f3ed34354436603d4c667c7779","body":{"detail":"The toggle reads site_access and site_url from GET /api/hosted/artifacts/<id>/sharing (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs get_sharing), and the Share button shows only where that route answers (web/shell/src/ui/Share.svelte). On a local daemon the owner opens a site to the world only with PATCH /api/artifacts/<id> {site_access} or an agent's publish_public site_access.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"718ea4de7247470d7c3e085992573d277be2dc4dd98ec31fa2f9436d07da4ee7"},"summary":"Only a hosted Clax's Share dialog offers Open to the world: a local daemon's shell has no toggle","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:32:22.613325Z","id":"2422cc43d11c5c3b633ffa6ccab769f248ace95f8af62e11dab3314cdce7e5ad","body":{"detail":"commentsOff(s) feeds the same readOnly prop a spectator's does (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte readOnly, ThreadCard.svelte), which hides reply, resolve, reopen and send. The daemon refuses only new threads and comments while the switch is off (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs refuse_comments_off_in); resolving and sending to an agent stay allowed. So the owner must turn Comments on to resolve old threads from the web. The page's comments capability (web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts commentable) refuses only the composer and posts, leaving resolve to the page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"14873dbc4e2ce7a209dafc6a0b89ba2a88ea2016f2932aa36412712ec331a2c6"},"suggested_fix":"Give Sidebar a narrower noReply prop that hides the reply box and the New comment box but keeps Resolve and Send, if the owner wants threads managed while comments are off.","summary":"With comments off the sidebar is read-only: no reply, and no Resolve, Reopen or Send on existing threads either","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/TopbarIsland.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:32:22.613514Z","id":"a648ffa6fa563454e0afcb960601f63d505b9a6a11e1ade1cef46d2c3c773d78","body":{"detail":"At 390 px wide the bar holds the mark, the title, the roster, Comment and the more menu; Get in Clax there squeezed the title to one letter (and off the bar beside a spectator count), so GetInClax.svelte hides at phone width and MoreMenu.svelte lists it first (getHref). On a phone, where Get in Clax opens the app by universal link, it is one tap further away.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"926b5967fe7496062c58aafda87bd14be8caa79186c8732467ea01ab6a8473cd"},"summary":"Get in Clax in the phone top bar rather than the more menu","tags":["app-push","revisit:the phone top bar gets room for a primary action, or app pages drop the roster at phone width","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/GetInClax.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:08.590469Z","id":"fabd6af40a34238c9d8f42643842482b0adc58b6c60de2d5f3046c4cc4a7db5d","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/theme.css:226 draws every top-bar button except .primary as a ghost; the only solid one today is Reload (TopbarIsland.svelte:65), shown only when a newer version is waiting. GetInClax.svelte copies button.primary's look (theme.css:106-107) unconditionally, so the owner's own app page has a permanent filled button between Fork and Share (and two filled buttons when Reload shows). For a visitor it is the page's call to action (spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull §5.5); for the owner, who already has the app, it outranks Share, the action they came for.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"9158ecfd66e0136478c59441755f2bec9326a94deca0114b4d22dd37ca370ea6"},"suggested_fix":"Draw it as the bar's ghost button for the owner's shell (TopbarIsland ownerShell) or whoever may share, and keep solid ink for visitors; or take button.primary's class rather than restating its rules.","summary":"Get in Clax is solid ink for every viewer, the owner included, where the bar's other actions are ghost buttons","tags":["app-push","ui","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:08.590525Z","id":"a2853df552c02451ec806406857a6ee16a47d96981a8e14ebda40b619fbf446e","body":{"detail":"TopbarIsland.svelte sets title=\"Comments are off for this page\" on the disabled Comment button, and the sidebar's empty state reads just \"Nothing open.\" (readOnly branch here). A title shows on mouse hover only, so a phone guest (390 px) sees a greyed Comment and an empty list with no reason; screen readers get it as the button's description. A spectator gets the same treatment, but a spectator's state is transient and the roster says \"viewing\"; comments off is a standing setting.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":264},"end":{"line":264},"content_hash":"aa399928898e78bc97fc9e60b849793fcbfa25392ade5dc9144b04a32f6733bc"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the reason into Sidebar (e.g. a note prop) and show \"Comments are off for this page.\" as the empty state, and above the list when threads exist, while ShellSidebar's commentsOff(s) holds.","summary":"With comments off, nothing on a phone says why Comment is dimmed: the reason is only in the button's title","tags":["app-push","ui","a11y","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:08.590675Z","id":"42f577cb538d55f2f3e7b0a7e1233fa7396ed95e3694239dfa6bcbc983e44d75","body":{"detail":"The input has role=switch and its label names it \"Comments\"; the line under it (data-testid=comments-note) is a sibling paragraph with no ID, so assistive tech does not read \"Off: nobody can comment, whatever their access.\" with the switch.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"89f91f2457bc02b481ffa3fadcd30eede7b22cbe525044032b597f0ba74f39b2"},"suggested_fix":"Give the note an ID and set aria-describedby on the input.","summary":"The Comments switch's note is not tied to it, so a screen reader hears \"Comments, switch, off\" without what off means","tags":["app-push","a11y","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:08.591326Z","id":"2fab3b2a4cc43315fe86702577e40be4a8450d8eed2b5ece3d02bfa87e9dd2ef","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull D4a says nobody can comment while the switch is off, and §5.6 says the remote refuses comment creation (thread or reply) and existing threads stay readable; it says nothing against managing them. The daemon matches that: crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs calls refuse_comments_off_in only on thread creation (line 912) and on adding a comment (line 1394), so resolve, reopen and send succeed, and the page's comments capability (web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts commentable) refuses only the composer and posts. Feeding commentsOff(s) into Sidebar's readOnly (ShellSidebar.svelte:55) also hides Resolve, Reopen and Send to <agent> on every card (ThreadCard.svelte:216-221), the Send N unsent bar (Sidebar.svelte:237-241) and selection checkboxes (Sidebar.svelte:210). Failure: the owner turns Comments on, a guest leaves three threads, the owner turns Comments off to stop more; in the web view the owner can no longer resolve those threads or send them to their agent until Comments is turned back on, which reopens commenting to everyone meanwhile. Matching D4a: a separate noReply flag that drops the New comment box and each card's reply form, leaving readOnly for spectators.","kind":"comment","references":"2422cc43d11c5c3b633ffa6ccab769f248ace95f8af62e11dab3314cdce7e5ad","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"14873dbc4e2ce7a209dafc6a0b89ba2a88ea2016f2932aa36412712ec331a2c6"},"summary":"Recommendation: block only new threads and replies while comments are off; keep Resolve, Reopen and Send for whoever's role allows them","tags":["app-push","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:47.202292Z","id":"7ee2f980f07d77af15f07e8752a3a85dbaaa9fbeff94de59093546a5dfa07475","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2422cc43d11c5c3b633ffa6ccab769f248ace95f8af62e11dab3314cdce7e5ad","summary":"Implemented as record 2fab3b2a recommends, pending the owner's decision: a noReply flag (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte, ThreadCard.svelte) drops only the New comment box and each card's reply box while comments are off; Resolve, Reopen, Send, the Send N unsent bar and ticking stay, and readOnly is a spectator's alone (ShellSidebar.svelte). Commit 6fb64b9d4. web/shell/src/topbar.test.ts 'with comments off, a thread keeps Resolve and Send but has no reply box' passes, and fails with commentsOff(s) fed back into readOnly or with ThreadCard's reply box shown under noReply. The choice stays the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/GetInClax.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:47.377191Z","id":"71ada29807dc7d73382ed295c525ef05fa7efed6b22d053292ba246167a3438f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6fb64b9d4","summary":"GetInClax takes ghost, which TopbarIsland sets for the owner's shell or whoever may share (shareOpen); solid ink stays for visitors. just web-test: //web:unit, typecheck, lint, bundle_size PASSED; just test-affected d523321fd: 111 tests pass (target/t6b.log). topbar.test.ts 'Get in Clax is solid ink for a visitor and a ghost for whoever may share' fails with the class dropped; e2e sharing.spec.ts checks the owner's link has the ghost class (target/t6b-shots/owner-app-1280-*.png).","supersedes":"fabd6af40a34238c9d8f42643842482b0adc58b6c60de2d5f3046c4cc4a7db5d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:47.459199Z","id":"16f121c58dcec2a6068aaa04abae06ea68fda5c14c5cb3c52878c06d5b2afb72","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6fb64b9d4","summary":"Sidebar's noReply carries the reason, and its empty Open list reads 'Comments are off for this page.' while ShellSidebar's commentsOff(s) holds. just web-test: //web:unit, typecheck, lint, bundle_size PASSED; just test-affected d523321fd: 111 tests pass (target/t6b.log). topbar.test.ts 'sidebar has no composer when comments off' expects that text and fails with the branch removed; e2e sharing.spec.ts checks it for a guest.","supersedes":"a2853df552c02451ec806406857a6ee16a47d96981a8e14ebda40b619fbf446e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:57.871597Z","id":"59e124b9792114feebc8f5f4cfb7781c45cc2da16d8476079ddfcb14f4f1e64c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6fb64b9d4","summary":"The switch has aria-describedby=share-comments-note, the note's ID. just web-test: //web:unit, typecheck, lint, bundle_size PASSED; just test-affected d523321fd: 111 tests pass (target/t6b.log). share.test.ts 'share dialog toggles comments' checks it and fails with the attribute removed.","supersedes":"42f577cb538d55f2f3e7b0a7e1233fa7396ed95e3694239dfa6bcbc983e44d75","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.099317Z","id":"bc09b63a66c900f2e5a0e07923dfe94949202ec63f0308376e8079d718dae634","body":{"detail":"noReply's text (ShellSidebar.svelte:57, \"Comments are off for this page.\") is used only as the empty Open list's line. When threads exist, the cards lose their reply boxes and the New comment box is gone with no explanation; the only other place is the disabled Comment button's title (TopbarIsland.svelte), which a phone never shows on hover and a disabled button never receives focus for. Record a2853df5's suggested fix asked for the note above the list when threads exist too; its resolve (16f121c5) covered the empty state alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":268},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"f9aea4acb0f26015f41d527f6ffb084cd53f94d9909af57f0367ddc4053842d1"},"suggested_fix":"Render p.noReply as a muted line at the top of the Open section whenever it is set, and keep the empty-state text as it is.","summary":"With comments off and threads open, nothing in the sidebar says comments are off; the reason shows only when the Open list is empty","tags":["app-push","ui","a11y","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.099449Z","id":"7de63386e1aa551ffecc314266f28b04678ba77992e3c6f7d612a9767b48a47d","body":{"detail":"noReply keeps Resolve, Reopen and Send for every viewer (ThreadCard.svelte actions, Sidebar.svelte send bar). docs/contract.md (the Comments switch) and crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs (commit 28b7f14ab) refuse a send 403 comments_off to anyone who may not resolve the artifact's threads, so for a Can comment viewer every Send click ends in \"Could not send: comments are off for this page\" (web/shell/src/topbar.test.ts 'a send refused comments_off (a commenter, while comments are off) says so'). The view does not know whether the viewer may resolve, so it cannot hide the button today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"85802361ba180e1cc60a98817f7b11afc8c795f957ea9acb2c5b94912289fd96"},"suggested_fix":"Have GET /api/artifacts/<id> (and the bootstrap) carry may_resolve, and hide Send and the unsent bar under noReply when it is false.","summary":"While comments are off a commenter is still offered Send to <agent> and the Send N unsent bar, which the daemon always refuses them","tags":["app-push","ui","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.099624Z","id":"0c8caee06197e01b820027c3de767e0de2d59fa28d05fc197b2a4939939b788e","body":{"detail":"toggleComments resets box.checked to data.comments after act(). act returns false, and data is not refreshed, both when the PUT fails and when the PUT succeeds but the follow-up api.sharing(id) fails: in the second case the switch shows the old state, the error shows at the foot of the dialog (line 167, under the people list, away from the switch), and onComments is not called, so the view's Comment button disagrees with the daemon until reload. A tap while another action is in flight (busy) also returns false and flips the switch back with no message.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":81},"content_hash":"7105c8661837be4473c75ca55adf0788075219c3ec60f71d799b417991f0a928"},"suggested_fix":"On a successful PUT, take the answer's {comments} into data and call onComments before reloading the rest; disable the switch while busy.","summary":"The Comments switch can show the old state after the change took, and a tap while the dialog is busy reverts silently","tags":["app-push","ui","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:53.967129Z","id":"e1f459704f7e6117fb4d75bfde67448c2fc33f4eb33e197f851b3b4f017e9007","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/api.ts Artifact carries may_fork and may_tag but nothing that says the viewer may resolve its threads; the server decides it in crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs (resolves(), used at :1336 and :1523 for refuse_send_comments_off). The fix needs GET /api/artifacts/<id> and the bootstrap to carry it (for example may_resolve), a crates/ change; once they do, ShellSidebar.svelte can pass Sidebar no Send and no unsent bar under noReply when it is false. The sidebar now says comments are off above open threads (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte, .no-reply), so a commenter at least sees why before a Send is refused.","kind":"comment","references":"7de63386e1aa551ffecc314266f28b04678ba77992e3c6f7d612a9767b48a47d","summary":"Still open: the view cannot tell a commenter from someone who may resolve, so it cannot hide Send","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.266156Z","id":"c593711b1996cf0b9a7c7e99d7aed5053e66bc7f5fd1211478d1323f47a8eefc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a560d0cbf","summary":"toggleComments takes the PUT's answer (setComments now returns comments) into data and calls onComments before the dialog reloads, and the switch is disabled while busy. Test 'share dialog shows and tells a Comments change that took though its reload failed, and takes no tap while busy' (web/shell/src/share.test.ts; its fake answers PUT /comments {artifact_id, comments} as the server does); //web:unit passes. Mutations: the old ShareDialog.svelte fails on disabled; the old toggle with disabled kept fails on the switch's state.","supersedes":"0c8caee06197e01b820027c3de767e0de2d59fa28d05fc197b2a4939939b788e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.339589Z","id":"be7cbf381cbc2ec89b753f8b91e15852d297aa629b9ce4dac7a896402084f64f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e99d55ff1","summary":"The Open section shows p.noReply (.no-reply) whenever open or addressed threads exist; the empty list's line is unchanged. topbar.test.ts 'with comments off, a thread keeps Resolve and Send but has no reply box' checks .section-open .no-reply; web/e2e/sharing.spec.ts (d75c82206) checks it in Chromium with a thread open. //web:unit and //web:e2e_rest (sharing.spec.ts) pass. Mutation: the old Sidebar.svelte fails the unit test (null .no-reply).","supersedes":"bc09b63a66c900f2e5a0e07923dfe94949202ec63f0308376e8079d718dae634","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T15:36:04.107278Z","id":"a77d7ddd4d8b53eb2bc721a4a02f15c8f5a1576f957b976be5cbe45e851cd63e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5bdcd65e8a8c73d450a8d7c075cc23e79f4b8d9e","summary":"Fixed in 5bdcd65e8: GET /api/artifacts/<id> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs, through threads::resolves) and the bootstrap (crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs, threads::browser_resolves) carry may_resolve; ShellSidebar passes Sidebar noSend while comments are off and may_resolve is false, which drops each card's Send, ticking and the Send unsent bar; docs/contract.md 'The Comments switch' says so. Tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_app_bundles.rs may_resolve_is_said_and_a_comments_switch_change_announced (owner true, commenter false), shell_boot.rs names_the_cookies_viewer_only (local viewer true; embeds_what_the_api_answers_and_never_the_token checks the bootstrap equals GET), golden_single_owner.rs (may_resolve true); web/shell/src/topbar.test.ts 'with comments off, a viewer who may not resolve gets no Send, no ticking and no Send unsent bar'. bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all //web:unit //web:lint: all pass. Mutation: with artifact['may_resolve'] not set, integration__4 fails at api_app_bundles.rs:962 (owner: may_resolve null) and shell_boot.rs:91; with ShellSidebar's noSend removed, the topbar test fails (expected true to be false).","supersedes":"7de63386e1aa551ffecc314266f28b04678ba77992e3c6f7d612a9767b48a47d","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewTile.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.221443Z","id":"92f0c33c40ed5ccad8de434fb2c695d02eb3bceb95bf85f260a695720af16e47","body":{"detail":"The tile replaces the header button (web/shell/src/ui/HeaderLinks.svelte no longer renders it): the mockups' header has none, and the tile is in the empty gallery too. Under a search or a tag filter the tile is not shown, so New is a clear away; at phone width the tile is the first card in one column.","kind":"alternative","summary":"Keep the header's New button beside the New artifact tile","tags":["claxbot","revisit:people miss New while searching or filtering","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewTile.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:42:39.357139Z","id":"26b4fd5df4c62f99eadbe3024075defeeab5a11918c6ebc1e99ac04c061c5ebd","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"92f0c33c40ed5ccad8de434fb2c695d02eb3bceb95bf85f260a695720af16e47","summary":"Changed since recorded: the tile now leads the first section shown (web/shell/src/ui/NeedsGroup.svelte when the Needs group shows, else the grid in web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte), under a search or a tag filter too; only a search or filter that matches nothing hides it with the grid.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.500362Z","id":"5edfe32d28f96212c165b78645bf9a2d26495fb4b2ae0aee7806afe79a719e69","body":{"detail":"The gallery loads every artifact the viewer sees once and filters in the browser, by name or ID without case (web/shell/src/view/tags-model.ts carriesAll), as the search does, so pressing a tag needs no request and the tag bar can list every tag in use. The daemon's ?tag= filter (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs list) matches the same way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"b2fff55d9c303464d4653c2eec552e73a69e8a3381a4c7323c1d0755ef2bddec"},"summary":"Filter the gallery by tag through GET /api/artifacts?tag= instead of over the list it has loaded","supersedes":"3bc02bcacc4f6216fef2eba072f6283881bf93310abbfa65ff65a3a03faee8ce","tags":["tags","revisit:the gallery stops loading every artifact at once (paging)","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.529990Z","id":"87d2597fa3f60113a36e339b6a50129bf51bc2a2d92eb96edb2b3d980fce4ead","body":{"detail":"A tag filter shows one list, pinned first then most recent, as a search does: the filter is a narrowing the viewer chose, and sections of two or three cards read as noise. The bar's pressed tags say what is shown.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"b2fff55d9c303464d4653c2eec552e73a69e8a3381a4c7323c1d0755ef2bddec"},"summary":"Keep the gallery's attention sections (Needs your eyes, Everything else) under a tag filter","supersedes":"e1e1e6204c83c759c87c49c3a87feb1e760c81ba0e259721bf8cd2607a4463fb","tags":["tags","revisit:owners ask to see what needs them within a tag","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/NewArtifactDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.556461Z","id":"112577b594bbb5761806ab9369cb46c9b697955cda20317967efe95058558d61","body":{"detail":"A send with no live target makes untargeted feedback rows (clax-store feedback.rs send_in), which a watch hands over only to the owner's agents (routes/watches.rs put: retarget unless a grant), never to a person's agent. The dialog leaves the brief unsent and gives a prompt (view/new-artifact.ts connectPrompt) that tells the agent to watch the artifact and read the brief thread itself, which works for any harness.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":87},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"1ce7b40f97634a1ddee812a5eab4a4ec58b9eb852e1bfa8e410d2d8921763f02"},"summary":"With no agent live, send the brief untargeted so the first agent to watch takes it","supersedes":"ece44c9f518e61ca5f13ba4b6a346c843d0fd48ef3deb0c78a42c8eca90cce36","tags":["revisit:agents following the prompt miss the brief","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Who.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.580458Z","id":"397afa0ddbb3a980e4dc8555764d48f1f66884f728bb794c7b88b21ba99d9c52","body":{"detail":"Below 700 px the pill (.who) may shrink with overflow: hidden so the top bar never scrolls sideways (with two people, three agents and '2 viewing' it was 394 px at 390, More pushed off screen). When it shrinks, the end of the pill, the 'N viewing' count and the last chips, is cut off with no sign. Options: drop the count below a width, cap the roster at one chip per side when there is a count, or move the count into the people panel at phone width.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"287c95888790091a5edf54e5d6200b30103768f5eca7a9e4fe919cc2c41c6668"},"summary":"At phone width a crowded people pill is clipped at its right edge, hiding the viewing count without an ellipsis","supersedes":"e5e0475f1ae5bd3a66d9fb8b0908587667586076d1b8277c1d770842b6af097e","tags":["ui","phone","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.605303Z","id":"d0c674540691f21e0400c2ed3198127360f757d3cfa9248adc176a6e50e905b0","body":{"detail":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs measures the People page's chunk (people) but not the Tags page's (TagsPage.svelte, TagForm.svelte) nor the tag editor's (ui/tag-editor.ts, TagPicker.svelte); they load lazily, and nothing gates their growth.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"1ce344d756eaa574fd64fe0937154b9531411cc8f9c0f48e8f5031dbbb337d9b"},"summary":"The Tags page's chunk has no bundle-size measure","supersedes":"7934d6b0144843ee12002b94d732c3532977fdc4e3c5f034ce3a6b0f6e87faca","tags":["tags","bundle","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Share.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:26.515661Z","id":"a8070f405f4f5231112b0c2426633226d6345abac82eb7d82b18f17160deab30","body":{"detail":"Share.svelte loads with the more menu after the first paint and asks sharing to decide whether to show Share. On a local daemon, which serves no /api/hosted route, that is one 404 per artifact view; on a hosted daemon one store read. It does not delay the first paint or comment mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"dbb107e1fe91721b632d7ece169ed3e065c0c10f9e6a63da75c13119b7805725"},"suggested_fix":"Carry can_share on GET /api/artifacts/<id> (the view already loads it) and drop the separate request.","summary":"Every artifact view asks GET /api/hosted/artifacts/<id>/sharing once after the first paint, and a local daemon answers it 404","supersedes":"80f9b7c21dedfd94fab5ffe067c29c7d32bc92184de7d0743b990e886811c241","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:27.378783Z","id":"7ef3e7ec82d6f2ed39fc54d0204e4f1a346e1b78b98cfd2e870b60a8fd82eef8","body":{"detail":"A person's pick composer and New comment box both put their draft under thread null, so the sidebar's writers box above the threads shows the name and the text but not the spot; the spot is outlined in the page only (the pick's live selection, web/shell/src/view/live-view.ts sendCursor). Naming the pick's quote or element beside the draft would need the anchor label in the live message.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":241},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"28d34fb6d6ebe7773ccca0a659a186acfdc8216af1eadaf1e7686682595fa979"},"summary":"Others' new comments say who writes, not what they are commenting on","supersedes":"00f770eed9b3caf67cd64dc137cd5ac1af16c0ee249e033ed59ef71f23b18caf","tags":["live-layers","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:27.582923Z","id":"3b8d62bfa07f9dc77ed66fa48469e89e7d228e78a29b4d9c505d90b457af3725","body":{"detail":"The toggle reads site_access and site_url from GET /api/hosted/artifacts/<id>/sharing (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs get_sharing), and the Share button shows only where that route answers (web/shell/src/ui/Share.svelte). On a local daemon the owner opens a site to the world only with PATCH /api/artifacts/<id> {site_access} or an agent's publish_public site_access.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"718ea4de7247470d7c3e085992573d277be2dc4dd98ec31fa2f9436d07da4ee7"},"summary":"Only a hosted Clax's Share dialog offers Open to the world: a local daemon's shell has no toggle","supersedes":"7a30c815cf44f6ba4f5d4651d2ffe94321b576f3ed34354436603d4c667c7779","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/shell-controls.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:24:04.674663Z","id":"d8173bfd0caf2e8fe5a764a41b8cdfe8bbd6385180f409a1fe63d0ed9a0388a8","body":{"detail":"`inView(el)` (whole=false) is true while any part of the control overlaps the clip box, so a half-clipped control keeps a ring overhanging the clip. It also calls `getComputedStyle` per ancestor on each call; web/shell/src/ui/coach-mark.ts calls it from every captured scroll and, while a ring is up, on every animation frame. The cost is bounded by the ring's six seconds and one ring at a time, and is not measured.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"2e92cf87e6d0ab0b11b742f1b4b5af223509859ee5076847f4b9235f9f2121dc"},"summary":"`inView` counts partial visibility and runs getComputedStyle for each ancestor on every call","tags":["revisit:a ring is seen overhanging a clipped control, or a frame profile shows the placement","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/PermissionsPanel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T04:45:57.413938Z","id":"18b1000beb40baee6c3fdfc22cea9668bb8b811293b88982c3008729d6a4f365","body":{"detail":"remember(true) (PermissionsPanel.svelte:91) sets sessionStorage clax.permissions.reopen:<id> before DELETE capability-approval/<name>, so the panel reopens after the reload the withdraw causes. When the withdraw succeeds but what is served does not shrink (the view does not reload) and the person leaves the tab without Close, the flag stays; the next load of that artifact in the same tab opens the panel once, and onMount (line 75) clears it. The flag is per tab and cleared on the first mount, so the cost is one unexpected panel open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"4f4e9f942665c798c8e3c24e5dd72e98a982f4f505de5a2be5e1652e044761d7"},"summary":"The Permissions panel's reopen flag can linger in a tab after a withdraw that does not reload","tags":["review","design","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/ui/HeaderLinks.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T15:38:04.587636Z","id":"91477b81137dcb244fadbb3e399857a29dac30353e93cd72e7367fa7b0826350","body":{"detail":"On the gallery's pages the config request, and so the overlay and its diagnostics recorder, starts only once the lazy module loads after the first paint (on / after the artifact list loads; never when that list fails, as for a person with no read right), so errors from the gallery's first moments are not recorded. Even the bare request (fetch and JSON, without the reading in web/shell/src/feedback/boot.ts) put the gallery entry at 31349 gzip bytes against its 31240 budget, which //web:bundle_size measured at 31236 without it (web/perf/bundle-budget.json). The artifact entry asks it first thing (web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts:21) within its budget.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":11},"content_hash":"836ad9255d1fc5488f79f3331b0cb9f104e6a08a592f09fd318195da08d9a3f2"},"summary":"Ask the feedback config from the gallery's eager entry (as the artifact entry does) rather than from the gallery's lazy module","tags":["feedback-loop","status:needs-decision","revisit:the gallery budget is raised or the gallery entry shrinks by 120 bytes","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
